{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MTM8k8J1F1FJnvcrVUbnvs","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (50.3KB). Full output saved to: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.claude-account2/projects/-Users-michelkerkmeester-worktrees-public-455-expansive-depth-integration/bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410/tool-results/bnb22qcnw.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n# ────────\nstate_write_protocol:\n  mechanism: \"append-gateway\"\n  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n  applies_to: \"every append_to_jsonl and append_jsonl directive in this workflow\"\n  refusal_handling: \"halt on exit 2; never fall back to a direct file write. Exit 1 on a row that is still routed through the gateway is a workflow defect and halts; the pinned_bookkeeping rows are recorded through bookkeeping_log and are never routed.\"\n  pinned_bookkeeping:\n    events: [config_warning, lock_released, pivot_confirm_accepted, manualStop, pivot_override_accepted, maxDurationReached]\n    directive: \"bookkeeping_log\"\n    handling: \"These rows are workflow bookkeeping that the review ledger schema pins to the legacy path: they have no lossless review-event target, so the gateway would refuse them with exit 1 and write nothing. They are never sent to the gateway. The step prints the row in its log line and continues; none of them is a halt condition.\"\n  contract: |\n    The directives below specify WHAT to record; this block specifies the mechanism. The gateway\n    authorizes the write against the mode's durable authority record, serialises it behind the\n    ledger fence, returns a receipt, and refreshes state_log from the ledger. Exit 0 means the\n    record is durable in the ledger and the refreshed state_log carries it. Exit 2 means it was\n    refused, and the refusal names the check that failed.\n\n    Writing state_log directly bypasses ordering, authorization, and the receipt. Two writers\n    can then interleave with no shared ordering, and a record nobody authorized carries no\n    receipt, so a later reader cannot tell an accepted record from an invented one. A refusal\n    is a halt, never a reason to write the file directly.\n\n    There is no direct-append exception. state_log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"4bb4ea9b-8372-4c10-9439-16f33577525c","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:06:14.556Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# ────────\nstate_write_protocol:\n  mechanism: \"append-gateway\"\n  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n  applies_to: \"every append_to_jsonl and append_jsonl directive in this workflow\"\n  refusal_handling: \"halt on exit 2; never fall back to a direct file write. Exit 1 on a row that is still routed through the gateway is a workflow defect and halts; the pinned_bookkeeping rows are recorded through bookkeeping_log and are never routed.\"\n  pinned_bookkeeping:\n    events: [config_warning, lock_released, pivot_confirm_accepted, manualStop, pivot_override_accepted, maxDurationReached]\n    directive: \"bookkeeping_log\"\n    handling: \"These rows are workflow bookkeeping that the review ledger schema pins to the legacy path: they have no lossless review-event target, so the gateway would refuse them with exit 1 and write nothing. They are never sent to the gateway. The step prints the row in its log line and continues; none of them is a halt condition.\"\n  contract: |\n    The directives below specify WHAT to record; this block specifies the mechanism. The gateway\n    authorizes the write against the mode's durable authority record, serialises it behind the\n    ledger fence, returns a receipt, and refreshes state_log from the ledger. Exit 0 means the\n    record is durable in the ledger and the refreshed state_log carries it. Exit 2 means it was\n    refused, and the refusal names the check that failed.\n\n    Writing state_log directly bypasses ordering, authorization, and the receipt. Two writers\n    can then interleave with no shared ordering, and a record nobody authorized carries no\n    receipt, so a later reader cannot tell an accepted record from an invented one. A refusal\n    is a halt, never a reason to write the file directly.\n\n    There is no direct-append exception. state_log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from\n    the ledger, so a row written beside it is dropped by the next refresh: the migration\n    marker, the recovery baseline, the iteration-error row and the claim-adjudication gate\n    row are canonical ledger events like every other record.\n\nstate_paths:\n  # Template paths document the canonical packet layout. Runtime resolution happens via\n  # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n  # root-local review/ and child phases keep local review/ packet dirs.\n  # Canonical root-spec write targets remain review/deep-review-config.json,\n  # review/deep-review-state.jsonl, and review/deep-review-findings-registry.json.\n  packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n  local_packet_dir: \"{spec_folder}/review\"\n  legacy_root_report: \"{spec_folder}/review-report.md\"\n  config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-config.json\"\n  state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n  findings_registry: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"\n  strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n  dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n  pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review-pause\"\n  lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review.lock\"\n  prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n  iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n  iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n  # Per-iteration structured delta stream — complement to the canonical state_log\n  # append. MUST contain at least one record with `type === \"iteration\"`; variants\n  # like `\"iteration_delta\"` are silently dropped by the reducer.\n  delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n  delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n  review_output: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n  resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n  archive_root: \"{artifact_archive_root}\"\n\n# ────────\n# WORKFLOW\n# ────────\n\ngate_defaults:\n  after_gate_refresh_lock:\n    action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately after the operator response\"\n    command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n    on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet, so run step_release_lock and stop rather than continue without it.\"\n\nworkflow:\n\n  step_resolve_artifact_root:\n    description: \"Resolve artifact directory — use fan-out lineage override when provided, else resolve from spec_folder\"\n    note: \"Root specs keep review artifacts directly in {spec_folder}/review/. Child phases and sub-phases keep local packet directories in {spec_folder}/review/{packet}/, and archives stay local at {spec_folder}/review-archive/{packet}/.\"\n    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n    if_present:\n      bind:\n        artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n        artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n        artifact_subfolder: null\n        artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n    if_absent:\n      command: \"node -e \\\"const { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/review-research-paths.cjs'); console.log(JSON.stringify(resolveArtifactRoot('{spec_folder}', 'review')));\\\"\"\n      outputs:\n        - artifact_root_dir: \"Resolved local review owner directory\"\n        - artifact_subfolder: \"Local packet subfolder ({ownerSlug}-pt-{NN}), else null\"\n        - artifact_dir: \"Resolved review packet directory for this target\"\n        - artifact_archive_root: \"Resolved local review archive directory for this target\"\n\n  step_bind_reducer_artifact_arg:\n    description: \"Keep the reducer on the lineage-owned artifact directory during fan-out\"\n    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n    if_present:\n      bind:\n        reducer_artifact_arg: \"--artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\"\n    if_absent:\n      bind:\n        reducer_artifact_arg: \"\"\n\n  step_bind_convergence_write_arg:\n    description: \"Keep the convergence step from writing on a dry run\"\n    note: \"step_graph_convergence runs on a dry run as a preview. A live run passes --record-blocked-stop, which makes convergence.cjs append a real row on a BLOCKED decision. A dry run writes nothing, so it passes --read-only instead, which also keeps the script from persisting the graph snapshot or appending its observability event.\"\n    branch_on: \"dry_run == true\"\n    if_dry_run:\n      bind:\n        convergence_write_arg: \"--read-only\"\n    if_live_run:\n      bind:\n        convergence_write_arg: \"--record-blocked-stop\"\n\n  phase_init:\n    purpose: Create all state files for the review session and resolve review scope\n    steps:\n\n      step_preflight_contract:\n        action: \"Validate required setup bindings and executable workflow contract before any file writes\"\n        verify:\n          - required_values_present: [review_target, review_target_type, review_dimensions, spec_folder, lineage_mode, max_iterations, convergence_threshold, convergence_mode, depth_mode, stop_policy]\n          - dry_run_normalized: \"Boolean true or false before workflow loading; absent flag resolves to false.\"\n          - spec_folder_is_within: \"specs/ or .opencode/specs/ (canonicalize alias roots before validation)\"\n          - unresolved_placeholders: \"FAIL if any user-facing template references placeholders not produced by earlier steps\"\n          - tool_contract: \"FAIL if executable steps reference tools outside the command allowlist\"\n          - extend_values: \"When extend is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), and extend_minutes when bound likewise. extend_minutes without extend, or extend with a lineage_mode other than auto or completed-continue, is a usage error. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock, with a usage error that names the flag.\"\n          - frontier_cap_values: \"When frontier_max_depth or frontier_max_nodes is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), else fail with 'Usage error (frontier-cap-value): --frontier-max-depth needs a positive integer' or the same for --frontier-max-nodes. Either one bound while depth_mode != 'expansive' fails with 'Usage error (frontier-cap-without-expansive): --frontier-max-depth only applies with --depth-mode=expansive' or the same for --frontier-max-nodes. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock.\"\n        on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL and report the missing binding or unsupported contract reference\"\n\n      step_create_directories:\n        action: \"Create spec folder and canonical review packet directories if they don't exist\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.prompt_dir} {state_paths.iteration_dir} {state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n\n      step_detect_resource_map:\n        action: \"Detect resource-map.md before config creation so init can persist coverage-gate state\"\n        inspect:\n          - \"{spec_folder}/resource-map.md\"\n        classify:\n          present: \"resource-map.md exists at init\"\n          absent: \"resource-map.md does not exist at init\"\n        outputs:\n          - resource_map_present: \"Boolean true when {spec_folder}/resource-map.md exists, else false\"\n          - resource_map_known_context: \"When present: concise resource-map snapshot for Known Context and charter framing. When absent: 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n\n      step_migrate_legacy_review_state:\n        action: \"Rehome legacy review artifacts into review/iterations before session classification\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        detect:\n          canonical_review_state:\n            - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n            - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n            - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n            - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n          legacy_review_state:\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause\"\n            - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n            - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report}\"\n          legacy_review_markers:\n            - \"scratch/deep-review-strategy.md exists\"\n            - \"scratch/deep-research-config.json declares mode == 'review' OR scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl contains mode == 'review'\"\n        migrate_only:\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json -> {state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl -> {state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md -> {state_paths.strategy}\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md -> {state_paths.dashboard}\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause -> {state_paths.pause_sentinel}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n          - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report} -> {state_paths.review_output}\"\n        on_canonical_present: \"Leave canonical review/ state untouched and do not overwrite it with legacy scratch artifacts.\"\n        on_legacy_detected: \"Move only the review-specific whitelist, print LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED and leave unrelated scratch files untouched. Nothing is appended here: an append before session classification would create the state log and turn a fresh packet into a partial one, and the moved state log was written without the ledger, so the gateway refuses every append to it until step_classify_session.on_moved_legacy_state adopts it.\"\n        on_conflict: \"If canonical review/ state and legacy scratch review state both exist but disagree, halt for operator repair instead of merging contradictory state.\"\n        outputs:\n          - legacy_migration_detected: \"true when the command printed LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED, else false\"\n          - migration_recorded: \"false; step_record_artifact_migration sets it once the migration row is appended\"\n        command: |\n          mkdir -p {state_paths.iteration_dir}\n          if [ ! -e {state_paths.config} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.state_log} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.strategy} ] && [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && ( [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] || [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] ); then\n            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json {state_paths.config}\n            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl {state_paths.state_log}\n            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md {state_paths.strategy}\n            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md {state_paths.dashboard}\n            find {spec_folder}/scratch -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\;\n            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause {state_paths.pause_sentinel}\n            [ -e {state_paths.legacy_root_report} ] && mv {state_paths.legacy_root_report} {state_paths.review_output}\n            echo \"LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED\"\n          fi\n          find {state_paths.local_packet_dir} -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\; 2>/dev/null || true\n\n      step_acquire_lock:\n        action: \"Acquire the single-writer advisory lock before session classification\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        ttl_ms: \"lock_ttl_ms = max(1800000, executor_timeout * 1000). executor_timeout is the bound dispatch timeout in seconds, 900 when unset. The lock is stale after twice this value, so it outlives the longest allowed dispatch.\"\n        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs acquire --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --packet-id {spec_folder} --ttl-ms {lock_ttl_ms}\"\n        on_acquire: \"Capture lock.ownerPid as captured_owner_pid and lock.acquireNonce as captured_acquire_nonce from the JSON output, and reuse both for every release below. If acquired=false, fail closed — another deep-review run already holds this packet. Under confirm, mode_overrides.confirm.lock_not_acquired applies instead.\"\n        note: \"Uses the promoted runtime/ loop-lock CLI (single source of truth: stale-lock reclaim, clean owner-scoped release). macOS/BSD locking is advisory — best-effort single-writer, not a hard mutex across host calls. Acquire reclaims a stale lock itself and reports the old holder under `reclaimed`. A lock is stale when its heartbeat is older than twice its TTL, or when its owning process is known to be dead. No confirmation step exists in either mode: log a `reclaimed` holder and continue.\"\n        # Lock-cleanup contract: the lock file MUST be released on every terminal exit path that follows acquisition.\n        # Runtimes honoring step_acquire_lock are required to perform this cleanup before halting or pausing.\n        on_halt:\n          action: \"Every terminal halt after the acquire runs step_release_lock before it returns control\"\n          command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; failures here are logged but do not block the halt\"\n        on_cancel:\n          action: \"Release the lock on user cancel or pause-sentinel detection before sentinel processing\"\n          command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; cancel completes regardless of cleanup result\"\n        on_workflow_exit:\n          action: \"Release the lock as the final step of any workflow exit path (success or failure)\"\n          command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; idempotent — safe to invoke when already released\"\n\n      step_extend_completed_run:\n        action: \"Extend a completed run in place, under the lock and before classification, so the classifier sees a resumable run\"\n        skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'completed-continue'\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        note: |\n          --extend=N continues a finished run in the same session and generation. The\n          duration clock counts wall-clock time since createdAt, idle time included, so the\n          new budget starts from whichever is later, the old budget or the time already\n          spent, and createdAt is never re-stamped. The event is appended before the\n          config is replaced, so a failed append leaves the run complete and untouched.\n        command: |\n          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          WORK_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-extend.XXXXXX\")\"\n          node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" extend-review \"{state_paths.config}\" \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \"{extend}\" \"{extend_minutes}\" \"$WORK_DIR\" > \"$WORK_DIR/result.json\" || { STATUS=$?; rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"; exit \"$STATUS\"; }\n          node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$WORK_DIR/event.json\" || { rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"; exit 1; }\n          mv \"$WORK_DIR/config.json\" \"{state_paths.config}\" || { rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"; exit 1; }\n          cat \"$WORK_DIR/result.json\"\n          rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"\n        outputs:\n          - continued_from_run: \"continuedFromRun from the JSON output\"\n          - max_iterations: \"newMaxIterations from the JSON output; it replaces the command default so the loop cap and the convergence script read the same ceiling\"\n          - extension_pending: \"true\"\n          - extension_warning: \"warning from the JSON output, null when none\"\n        on_warning: \"When extension_warning is not null, print it and continue. It never refuses the extension.\"\n        on_fail: \"Exit 2 is a usage error, such as a run that is not complete: halt with that message through step_release_lock and leave the config untouched. Any other failure halts with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock.\"\n\n      step_snapshot_extended_review_report:\n        action: \"Keep the prior review report before the extension's first dispatch, so re-synthesis cannot overwrite it\"\n        skip_when: \"extension_pending != true\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        command: |\n          GENERATION=\"$(node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/workflow-steps.cjs generation \"{state_paths.config}\")\" || exit 1\n          SNAPSHOT=\"{state_paths.packet_dir}/review-report-v${GENERATION}-r{continued_from_run}.md\"\n          if [ -e \"$SNAPSHOT\" ]; then\n            echo \"The review report snapshot $SNAPSHOT is already there.\" >&2\n            exit 1\n          fi\n          if [ -f \"{state_paths.review_output}\" ]; then\n            cp \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \"$SNAPSHOT\"\n          fi\n        note: \"Keyed by generation and continuedFromRun, so a second extension of the same generation writes its own snapshot.\"\n        on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. Never overwrite an existing snapshot.\"\n\n      step_classify_session:\n        action: \"Classify the session before writing files\"\n        inspect:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        classify:\n          fresh: \"None of the three state artifacts exist\"\n          resume: \"Config, JSONL, and strategy all exist and config.mode == 'review' and agree on target/spec folder\"\n          completed-session: \"Resume artifacts exist and config.status == 'complete'\"\n          invalid-state: \"Any partial, missing, or contradictory combination\"\n        extension_rule: \"When extension_pending == true, step_extend_completed_run has just set status initialized and appended run_extended, so a synthesis_complete row followed by an extended row is consistent: classify as resume, never as invalid-state or completed-session.\"\n        outputs:\n          - session_state: \"fresh | resume | completed-session | invalid-state\"\n          - prior_tail_digest: \"sha256 of the state log bytes when resuming or restarting an existing lineage\"\n        lifecycle_routing:\n          - \"If lineage_mode == restart, step_apply_lifecycle_request archived the packet before the lock was taken, so session_state is fresh and on_fresh runs.\"\n          - \"If lineage_mode == auto or lineage_mode == resume, preserve the existing resume/completed/fresh behavior.\"\n        on_resume:\n          before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n          log: \"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent. Continue the same lineage (sessionId unchanged, generation unchanged, no archive).\"\n          append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_resumed\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"sourceSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"resumeReason\":\"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent; continue the same lineage.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n          extension_override: \"When extension_pending == true, skip this append_jsonl: step_extend_completed_run already recorded the lifecycle action as run_extended, so the ledger carries one event per action. Keep lineage_mode completed-continue and skip_to phase_loop.\"\n          skip_to: phase_loop\n          confirm_choice:\n            applies_to: confirm\n            preempts: \"Under confirm this block runs in place of the sibling log, append_jsonl and skip_to keys of on_resume. Under auto it is skipped and those keys run.\"\n            show_dashboard: \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n            ask: \"Existing review session is consistent. Resume where it left off, or restart (archive the current review packet under the root-level review-archive/ tree and start a fresh session)?\"\n            after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n            options: [resume, restart, cancel]\n            on_resume_choice:\n              dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n              before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n              set:\n                lineage_mode: \"resume\"\n                parent_session_id: \"{session_id}\"\n              append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_resumed\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"sourceSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"resumeReason\":\"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent; continue the same lineage.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n              skip_to: gate_init_approval\n              extension_override: \"When extension_pending == true, do not set lineage_mode to resume and do not append the resumed row, because run_extended already records this extension. Keep lineage_mode completed-continue and skip_to gate_init_approval.\"\n            on_restart_choice:\n              dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n              bind_prior_lineage:\n                action: \"Read the session id and generation of the packet that is about to be archived\"\n                command: |\n                  node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/workflow-steps.cjs prior-lineage \"{state_paths.config}\" \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n                outputs:\n                  - prior_session_id: \"priorSessionId from the JSON output, null when no old config exists\"\n                  - prior_generation: \"priorGeneration from the JSON output, 0 when no old config exists\"\n                  - prior_tail_digest: \"priorTailDigest from the JSON output: the sha256 of the old state log bytes, or of zero bytes when no old state log exists\"\n                on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. The old config is unreadable, so repair or archive the packet by hand.\"\n              command: |\n                if [ -e \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\" ]; then\n                  echo \"The archive folder {state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug} is already there.\" >&2\n                  exit 1\n                fi\n                mkdir -p \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\" || exit 1\n                find \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 ! -name \"$(basename \"{state_paths.lock_file}\")\" -exec mv {} \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}/\" \\; || exit 1\n                mkdir -p \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}\" \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}\" \"{state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n              on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. Never fall back to resume.\"\n              set:\n                lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n              skip_to: step_create_config\n            on_cancel_choice:\n              halt: true\n              release_lock: step_release_lock\n              message: \"Review session preserved. Manually archive or edit review/ before re-running.\"\n        on_restart:\n          action: \"Nothing is archived here. step_apply_lifecycle_request archived the packet before the lock was taken, so a restart run reaches this step as fresh and continues as on_fresh.\"\n        note_deferred_branches: \"fork is deferred and not runtime-supported in this release.\"\n        note_live_branches: \"completed-continue is live through --extend=N: step_extend_completed_run reopens a completed run before classification, so it lands here as resume. The live modes are new, resume, restart and completed-continue. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches for the one-session contract.\"\n        on_moved_legacy_state:\n          applies_when: \"legacy_migration_detected == true and the branch taken resumes the session or goes to synthesis; never on restart or cancel\"\n          order: \"Runs after classification and before that branch appends anything, the resume event included.\"\n          note: |\n            The state log moved out of scratch/ was written by hand before the ledger existed, so the\n            gateway refuses every append to it. Set it aside unchanged as deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl,\n            open the run from the moved config, then replay its iteration rows through the gateway,\n            which carries each one whole. Rows the gateway cannot carry stay only in the set-aside file,\n            and the replay reports how many. Exit 2 from any of the three is a halt.\n          set_aside_command: |\n            STATE_LOG=\"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n            LEGACY_LOG=\"$(dirname \"$STATE_LOG\")/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\"\n            if [ -e \"$LEGACY_LOG\" ]; then\n              echo \"A set-aside legacy state log already exists at $LEGACY_LOG. Repair the packet by hand.\" >&2\n              exit 1\n            fi\n            mv \"$STATE_LOG\" \"$LEGACY_LOG\"\n          open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n          replay_command: |\n            GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n            [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n            RUN_DIR=\"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\"\n            node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" replay-legacy-review \"$GATEWAY\" \"$RUN_DIR/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\" \"$RUN_DIR\"\n        on_completed_session:\n          before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n          log: \"Prior session already completed. Either archive the completed review/ tree and start a fresh session, or jump straight to synthesis with the existing artifacts.\"\n          skip_to: phase_synthesis\n        on_invalid_state:\n          halt: true\n          release_lock: step_release_lock\n          message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n        on_fresh:\n          action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n\n      step_scope_discovery:\n        action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n        resolve:\n          spec-folder: |\n            1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, acceptance-criteria.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n            2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n            3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n            4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n            5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n            6. Set scope = the packet's own canonical docs plus all discovered implementation and test files\n          skill: |\n            1. Read SKILL.md from .skilled/skills/{skill_name}/","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/.claude-account2/projects/-Users-michelkerkmeester-worktrees-public-455-expansive-depth-integration/bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410/tool-results/bnb22qcnw.txt","persistedOutputSize":51532},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MTM8k8J1F1FJnvcrVUbnvs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChEhjbEV1R1bxz2BCKDXq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VafqANg62ZbHggE3k5AzrF","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/.claude-account2/projects/-Users-michelkerkmeester-worktrees-public-455-expansive-depth-integration/bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410/tool-results/bnb22qcnw.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":973,"cache_read_input_tokens":73568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":973},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"95df9962-e345-4b8f-b498-b0defd7875a8","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:06:17.508Z","request_id":"req_011ChEhjb6Y6jwDu3NX5szbq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VafqANg62ZbHggE3k5AzrF":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/.claude-account2/projects/-Users-michelkerkmeester-worktrees-public-455-expansive-depth-integration/bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410/tool-results/bnb22qcnw.txt"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VafqANg62ZbHggE3k5AzrF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ────────\n2\tstate_write_protocol:\n3\t  mechanism: \"append-gateway\"\n4\t  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n5\t  applies_to: \"every append_to_jsonl and append_jsonl directive in this workflow\"\n6\t  refusal_handling: \"halt on exit 2; never fall back to a direct file write. Exit 1 on a row that is still routed through the gateway is a workflow defect and halts; the pinned_bookkeeping rows are recorded through bookkeeping_log and are never routed.\"\n7\t  pinned_bookkeeping:\n8\t    events: [config_warning, lock_released, pivot_confirm_accepted, manualStop, pivot_override_accepted, maxDurationReached]\n9\t    directive: \"bookkeeping_log\"\n10\t    handling: \"These rows are workflow bookkeeping that the review ledger schema pins to the legacy path: they have no lossless review-event target, so the gateway would refuse them with exit 1 and write nothing. They are never sent to the gateway. The step prints the row in its log line and continues; none of them is a halt condition.\"\n11\t  contract: |\n12\t    The directives below specify WHAT to record; this block specifies the mechanism. The gateway\n13\t    authorizes the write against the mode's durable authority record, serialises it behind the\n14\t    ledger fence, returns a receipt, and refreshes state_log from the ledger. Exit 0 means the\n15\t    record is durable in the ledger and the refreshed state_log carries it. Exit 2 means it was\n16\t    refused, and the refusal names the check that failed.\n17\t\n18\t    Writing state_log directly bypasses ordering, authorization, and the receipt. Two writers\n19\t    can then interleave with no shared ordering, and a record nobody authorized carries no\n20\t    receipt, so a later reader cannot tell an accepted record from an invented one. A refusal\n21\t    is a halt, never a reason to write the file directly.\n22\t\n23\t    There is no direct-append exception. state_log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from\n24\t    the ledger, so a row written beside it is dropped by the next refresh: the migration\n25\t    marker, the recovery baseline, the iteration-error row and the claim-adjudication gate\n26\t    row are canonical ledger events like every other record.\n27\t\n28\tstate_paths:\n29\t  # Template paths document the canonical packet layout. Runtime resolution happens via\n30\t  # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n31\t  # root-local review/ and child phases keep local review/ packet dirs.\n32\t  # Canonical root-spec write targets remain review/deep-review-config.json,\n33\t  # review/deep-review-state.jsonl, and review/deep-review-findings-registry.json.\n34\t  packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n35\t  local_packet_dir: \"{spec_folder}/review\"\n36\t  legacy_root_report: \"{spec_folder}/review-report.md\"\n37\t  config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-config.json\"\n38\t  state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n39\t  findings_registry: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"\n40\t  strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n41\t  dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n42\t  pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review-pause\"\n43\t  lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review.lock\"\n44\t  prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n45\t  iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n46\t  iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n47\t  # Per-iteration structured delta stream — complement to the canonical state_log\n48\t  # append. MUST contain at least one record with `type === \"iteration\"`; variants\n49\t  # like `\"iteration_delta\"` are silently dropped by the reducer.\n50\t  delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n51\t  delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n52\t  review_output: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n53\t  resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n54\t  archive_root: \"{artifact_archive_root}\"\n55\t\n56\t# ────────\n57\t# WORKFLOW\n58\t# ────────\n59\t\n60\tgate_defaults:\n61\t  after_gate_refresh_lock:\n62\t    action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately after the operator response\"\n63\t    command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n64\t    on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet, so run step_release_lock and stop rather than continue without it.\"\n65\t\n66\tworkflow:\n67\t\n68\t  step_resolve_artifact_root:\n69\t    description: \"Resolve artifact directory — use fan-out lineage override when provided, else resolve from spec_folder\"\n70\t    note: \"Root specs keep review artifacts directly in {spec_folder}/review/. Child phases and sub-phases keep local packet directories in {spec_folder}/review/{packet}/, and archives stay local at {spec_folder}/review-archive/{packet}/.\"\n71\t    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n72\t    if_present:\n73\t      bind:\n74\t        artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n75\t        artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n76\t        artifact_subfolder: null\n77\t        artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n78\t    if_absent:\n79\t      command: \"node -e \\\"const { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/review-research-paths.cjs'); console.log(JSON.stringify(resolveArtifactRoot('{spec_folder}', 'review')));\\\"\"\n80\t      outputs:\n81\t        - artifact_root_dir: \"Resolved local review owner directory\"\n82\t        - artifact_subfolder: \"Local packet subfolder ({ownerSlug}-pt-{NN}), else null\"\n83\t        - artifact_dir: \"Resolved review packet directory for this target\"\n84\t        - artifact_archive_root: \"Resolved local review archive directory for this target\"\n85\t\n86\t  step_bind_reducer_artifact_arg:\n87\t    description: \"Keep the reducer on the lineage-owned artifact directory during fan-out\"\n88\t    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n89\t    if_present:\n90\t      bind:\n91\t        reducer_artifact_arg: \"--artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\"\n92\t    if_absent:\n93\t      bind:\n94\t        reducer_artifact_arg: \"\"\n95\t\n96\t  step_bind_convergence_write_arg:\n97\t    description: \"Keep the convergence step from writing on a dry run\"\n98\t    note: \"step_graph_convergence runs on a dry run as a preview. A live run passes --record-blocked-stop, which makes convergence.cjs append a real row on a BLOCKED decision. A dry run writes nothing, so it passes --read-only instead, which also keeps the script from persisting the graph snapshot or appending its observability event.\"\n99\t    branch_on: \"dry_run == true\"\n100\t    if_dry_run:\n101\t      bind:\n102\t        convergence_write_arg: \"--read-only\"\n103\t    if_live_run:\n104\t      bind:\n105\t        convergence_write_arg: \"--record-blocked-stop\"\n106\t\n107\t  phase_init:\n108\t    purpose: Create all state files for the review session and resolve review scope\n109\t    steps:\n110\t\n111\t      step_preflight_contract:\n112\t        action: \"Validate required setup bindings and executable workflow contract before any file writes\"\n113\t        verify:\n114\t          - required_values_present: [review_target, review_target_type, review_dimensions, spec_folder, lineage_mode, max_iterations, convergence_threshold, convergence_mode, depth_mode, stop_policy]\n115\t          - dry_run_normalized: \"Boolean true or false before workflow loading; absent flag resolves to false.\"\n116\t          - spec_folder_is_within: \"specs/ or .opencode/specs/ (canonicalize alias roots before validation)\"\n117\t          - unresolved_placeholders: \"FAIL if any user-facing template references placeholders not produced by earlier steps\"\n118\t          - tool_contract: \"FAIL if executable steps reference tools outside the command allowlist\"\n119\t          - extend_values: \"When extend is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), and extend_minutes when bound likewise. extend_minutes without extend, or extend with a lineage_mode other than auto or completed-continue, is a usage error. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock, with a usage error that names the flag.\"\n120\t          - frontier_cap_values: \"When frontier_max_depth or frontier_max_nodes is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), else fail with 'Usage error (frontier-cap-value): --frontier-max-depth needs a positive integer' or the same for --frontier-max-nodes. Either one bound while depth_mode != 'expansive' fails with 'Usage error (frontier-cap-without-expansive): --frontier-max-depth only applies with --depth-mode=expansive' or the same for --frontier-max-nodes. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock.\"\n121\t        on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL and report the missing binding or unsupported contract reference\"\n122\t\n123\t      step_create_directories:\n124\t        action: \"Create spec folder and canonical review packet directories if they don't exist\"\n125\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n126\t        command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.prompt_dir} {state_paths.iteration_dir} {state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n127\t\n128\t      step_detect_resource_map:\n129\t        action: \"Detect resource-map.md before config creation so init can persist coverage-gate state\"\n130\t        inspect:\n131\t          - \"{spec_folder}/resource-map.md\"\n132\t        classify:\n133\t          present: \"resource-map.md exists at init\"\n134\t          absent: \"resource-map.md does not exist at init\"\n135\t        outputs:\n136\t          - resource_map_present: \"Boolean true when {spec_folder}/resource-map.md exists, else false\"\n137\t          - resource_map_known_context: \"When present: concise resource-map snapshot for Known Context and charter framing. When absent: 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n138\t\n139\t      step_migrate_legacy_review_state:\n140\t        action: \"Rehome legacy review artifacts into review/iterations before session classification\"\n141\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n142\t        detect:\n143\t          canonical_review_state:\n144\t            - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n145\t            - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n146\t            - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n147\t            - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n148\t          legacy_review_state:\n149\t            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json\"\n150\t            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n151\t            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n152\t            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n153\t            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md\"\n154\t            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause\"\n155\t            - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n156\t            - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report}\"\n157\t          legacy_review_markers:\n158\t            - \"scratch/deep-review-strategy.md exists\"\n159\t            - \"scratch/deep-research-config.json declares mode == 'review' OR scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl contains mode == 'review'\"\n160\t        migrate_only:\n161\t          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json -> {state_paths.config}\"\n162\t          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl -> {state_paths.state_log}\"\n163\t          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md -> {state_paths.strategy}\"\n164\t          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md -> {state_paths.dashboard}\"\n165\t          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n166\t          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause -> {state_paths.pause_sentinel}\"\n167\t          - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n168\t          - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report} -> {state_paths.review_output}\"\n169\t        on_canonical_present: \"Leave canonical review/ state untouched and do not overwrite it with legacy scratch artifacts.\"\n170\t        on_legacy_detected: \"Move only the review-specific whitelist, print LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED and leave unrelated scratch files untouched. Nothing is appended here: an append before session classification would create the state log and turn a fresh packet into a partial one, and the moved state log was written without the ledger, so the gateway refuses every append to it until step_classify_session.on_moved_legacy_state adopts it.\"\n171\t        on_conflict: \"If canonical review/ state and legacy scratch review state both exist but disagree, halt for operator repair instead of merging contradictory state.\"\n172\t        outputs:\n173\t          - legacy_migration_detected: \"true when the command printed LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED, else false\"\n174\t          - migration_recorded: \"false; step_record_artifact_migration sets it once the migration row is appended\"\n175\t        command: |\n176\t          mkdir -p {state_paths.iteration_dir}\n177\t          if [ ! -e {state_paths.config} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.state_log} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.strategy} ] && [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && ( [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] || [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] ); then\n178\t            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json {state_paths.config}\n179\t            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl {state_paths.state_log}\n180\t            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md {state_paths.strategy}\n181\t            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md {state_paths.dashboard}\n182\t            find {spec_folder}/scratch -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\;\n183\t            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause {state_paths.pause_sentinel}\n184\t            [ -e {state_paths.legacy_root_report} ] && mv {state_paths.legacy_root_report} {state_paths.review_output}\n185\t            echo \"LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED\"\n186\t          fi\n187\t          find {state_paths.local_packet_dir} -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\; 2>/dev/null || true\n188\t\n189\t      step_acquire_lock:\n190\t        action: \"Acquire the single-writer advisory lock before session classification\"\n191\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n192\t        ttl_ms: \"lock_ttl_ms = max(1800000, executor_timeout * 1000). executor_timeout is the bound dispatch timeout in seconds, 900 when unset. The lock is stale after twice this value, so it outlives the longest allowed dispatch.\"\n193\t        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs acquire --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --packet-id {spec_folder} --ttl-ms {lock_ttl_ms}\"\n194\t        on_acquire: \"Capture lock.ownerPid as captured_owner_pid and lock.acquireNonce as captured_acquire_nonce from the JSON output, and reuse both for every release below. If acquired=false, fail closed — another deep-review run already holds this packet. Under confirm, mode_overrides.confirm.lock_not_acquired applies instead.\"\n195\t        note: \"Uses the promoted runtime/ loop-lock CLI (single source of truth: stale-lock reclaim, clean owner-scoped release). macOS/BSD locking is advisory — best-effort single-writer, not a hard mutex across host calls. Acquire reclaims a stale lock itself and reports the old holder under `reclaimed`. A lock is stale when its heartbeat is older than twice its TTL, or when its owning process is known to be dead. No confirmation step exists in either mode: log a `reclaimed` holder and continue.\"\n196\t        # Lock-cleanup contract: the lock file MUST be released on every terminal exit path that follows acquisition.\n197\t        # Runtimes honoring step_acquire_lock are required to perform this cleanup before halting or pausing.\n198\t        on_halt:\n199\t          action: \"Every terminal halt after the acquire runs step_release_lock before it returns control\"\n200\t          command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; failures here are logged but do not block the halt\"\n201\t        on_cancel:\n202\t          action: \"Release the lock on user cancel or pause-sentinel detection before sentinel processing\"\n203\t          command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; cancel completes regardless of cleanup result\"\n204\t        on_workflow_exit:\n205\t          action: \"Release the lock as the final step of any workflow exit path (success or failure)\"\n206\t          command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; idempotent — safe to invoke when already released\"\n207\t\n208\t      step_extend_completed_run:\n209\t        action: \"Extend a completed run in place, under the lock and before classification, so the classifier sees a resumable run\"\n210\t        skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'completed-continue'\"\n211\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n212\t        note: |\n213\t          --extend=N continues a finished run in the same session and generation. The\n214\t          duration clock counts wall-clock time since createdAt, idle time included, so the\n215\t          new budget starts from whichever is later, the old budget or the time already\n216\t          spent, and createdAt is never re-stamped. The event is appended before the\n217\t          config is replaced, so a failed append leaves the run complete and untouched.\n218\t        command: |\n219\t          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n220\t          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n221\t          WORK_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-extend.XXXXXX\")\"\n222\t          node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" extend-review \"{state_paths.config}\" \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \"{extend}\" \"{extend_minutes}\" \"$WORK_DIR\" > \"$WORK_DIR/result.json\" || { STATUS=$?; rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"; exit \"$STATUS\"; }\n223\t          node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$WORK_DIR/event.json\" || { rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"; exit 1; }\n224\t          mv \"$WORK_DIR/config.json\" \"{state_paths.config}\" || { rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"; exit 1; }\n225\t          cat \"$WORK_DIR/result.json\"\n226\t          rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"\n227\t        outputs:\n228\t          - continued_from_run: \"continuedFromRun from the JSON output\"\n229\t          - max_iterations: \"newMaxIterations from the JSON output; it replaces the command default so the loop cap and the convergence script read the same ceiling\"\n230\t          - extension_pending: \"true\"\n231\t          - extension_warning: \"warning from the JSON output, null when none\"\n232\t        on_warning: \"When extension_warning is not null, print it and continue. It never refuses the extension.\"\n233\t        on_fail: \"Exit 2 is a usage error, such as a run that is not complete: halt with that message through step_release_lock and leave the config untouched. Any other failure halts with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock.\"\n234\t\n235\t      step_snapshot_extended_review_report:\n236\t        action: \"Keep the prior review report before the extension's first dispatch, so re-synthesis cannot overwrite it\"\n237\t        skip_when: \"extension_pending != true\"\n238\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n239\t        command: |\n240\t          GENERATION=\"$(node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/workflow-steps.cjs generation \"{state_paths.config}\")\" || exit 1\n241\t          SNAPSHOT=\"{state_paths.packet_dir}/review-report-v${GENERATION}-r{continued_from_run}.md\"\n242\t          if [ -e \"$SNAPSHOT\" ]; then\n243\t            echo \"The review report snapshot $SNAPSHOT is already there.\" >&2\n244\t            exit 1\n245\t          fi\n246\t          if [ -f \"{state_paths.review_output}\" ]; then\n247\t            cp \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \"$SNAPSHOT\"\n248\t          fi\n249\t        note: \"Keyed by generation and continuedFromRun, so a second extension of the same generation writes its own snapshot.\"\n250\t        on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. Never overwrite an existing snapshot.\"\n251\t\n252\t      step_classify_session:\n253\t        action: \"Classify the session before writing files\"\n254\t        inspect:\n255\t          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n256\t          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n257\t          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n258\t          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n259\t        classify:\n260\t          fresh: \"None of the three state artifacts exist\"\n261\t          resume: \"Config, JSONL, and strategy all exist and config.mode == 'review' and agree on target/spec folder\"\n262\t          completed-session: \"Resume artifacts exist and config.status == 'complete'\"\n263\t          invalid-state: \"Any partial, missing, or contradictory combination\"\n264\t        extension_rule: \"When extension_pending == true, step_extend_completed_run has just set status initialized and appended run_extended, so a synthesis_complete row followed by an extended row is consistent: classify as resume, never as invalid-state or completed-session.\"\n265\t        outputs:\n266\t          - session_state: \"fresh | resume | completed-session | invalid-state\"\n267\t          - prior_tail_digest: \"sha256 of the state log bytes when resuming or restarting an existing lineage\"\n268\t        lifecycle_routing:\n269\t          - \"If lineage_mode == restart, step_apply_lifecycle_request archived the packet before the lock was taken, so session_state is fresh and on_fresh runs.\"\n270\t          - \"If lineage_mode == auto or lineage_mode == resume, preserve the existing resume/completed/fresh behavior.\"\n271\t        on_resume:\n272\t          before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n273\t          log: \"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent. Continue the same lineage (sessionId unchanged, generation unchanged, no archive).\"\n274\t          append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_resumed\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"sourceSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"resumeReason\":\"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent; continue the same lineage.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n275\t          extension_override: \"When extension_pending == true, skip this append_jsonl: step_extend_completed_run already recorded the lifecycle action as run_extended, so the ledger carries one event per action. Keep lineage_mode completed-continue and skip_to phase_loop.\"\n276\t          skip_to: phase_loop\n277\t          confirm_choice:\n278\t            applies_to: confirm\n279\t            preempts: \"Under confirm this block runs in place of the sibling log, append_jsonl and skip_to keys of on_resume. Under auto it is skipped and those keys run.\"\n280\t            show_dashboard: \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n281\t            ask: \"Existing review session is consistent. Resume where it left off, or restart (archive the current review packet under the root-level review-archive/ tree and start a fresh session)?\"\n282\t            after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n283\t            options: [resume, restart, cancel]\n284\t            on_resume_choice:\n285\t              dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n286\t              before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n287\t              set:\n288\t                lineage_mode: \"resume\"\n289\t                parent_session_id: \"{session_id}\"\n290\t              append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_resumed\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"sourceSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"resumeReason\":\"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent; continue the same lineage.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n291\t              skip_to: gate_init_approval\n292\t              extension_override: \"When extension_pending == true, do not set lineage_mode to resume and do not append the resumed row, because run_extended already records this extension. Keep lineage_mode completed-continue and skip_to gate_init_approval.\"\n293\t            on_restart_choice:\n294\t              dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n295\t              bind_prior_lineage:\n296\t                action: \"Read the session id and generation of the packet that is about to be archived\"\n297\t                command: |\n298\t                  node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/workflow-steps.cjs prior-lineage \"{state_paths.config}\" \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n299\t                outputs:\n300\t                  - prior_session_id: \"priorSessionId from the JSON output, null when no old config exists\"\n301\t                  - prior_generation: \"priorGeneration from the JSON output, 0 when no old config exists\"\n302\t                  - prior_tail_digest: \"priorTailDigest from the JSON output: the sha256 of the old state log bytes, or of zero bytes when no old state log exists\"\n303\t                on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. The old config is unreadable, so repair or archive the packet by hand.\"\n304\t              command: |\n305\t                if [ -e \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\" ]; then\n306\t                  echo \"The archive folder {state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug} is already there.\" >&2\n307\t                  exit 1\n308\t                fi\n309\t                mkdir -p \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\" || exit 1\n310\t                find \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 ! -name \"$(basename \"{state_paths.lock_file}\")\" -exec mv {} \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}/\" \\; || exit 1\n311\t                mkdir -p \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}\" \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}\" \"{state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n312\t              on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. Never fall back to resume.\"\n313\t              set:\n314\t                lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n315\t              skip_to: step_create_config\n316\t            on_cancel_choice:\n317\t              halt: true\n318\t              release_lock: step_release_lock\n319\t              message: \"Review session preserved. Manually archive or edit review/ before re-running.\"\n320\t        on_restart:\n321\t          action: \"Nothing is archived here. step_apply_lifecycle_request archived the packet before the lock was taken, so a restart run reaches this step as fresh and continues as on_fresh.\"\n322\t        note_deferred_branches: \"fork is deferred and not runtime-supported in this release.\"\n323\t        note_live_branches: \"completed-continue is live through --extend=N: step_extend_completed_run reopens a completed run before classification, so it lands here as resume. The live modes are new, resume, restart and completed-continue. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches for the one-session contract.\"\n324\t        on_moved_legacy_state:\n325\t          applies_when: \"legacy_migration_detected == true and the branch taken resumes the session or goes to synthesis; never on restart or cancel\"\n326\t          order: \"Runs after classification and before that branch appends anything, the resume event included.\"\n327\t          note: |\n328\t            The state log moved out of scratch/ was written by hand before the ledger existed, so the\n329\t            gateway refuses every append to it. Set it aside unchanged as deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl,\n330\t            open the run from the moved config, then replay its iteration rows through the gateway,\n331\t            which carries each one whole. Rows the gateway cannot carry stay only in the set-aside file,\n332\t            and the replay reports how many. Exit 2 from any of the three is a halt.\n333\t          set_aside_command: |\n334\t            STATE_LOG=\"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n335\t            LEGACY_LOG=\"$(dirname \"$STATE_LOG\")/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\"\n336\t            if [ -e \"$LEGACY_LOG\" ]; then\n337\t              echo \"A set-aside legacy state log already exists at $LEGACY_LOG. Repair the packet by hand.\" >&2\n338\t              exit 1\n339\t            fi\n340\t            mv \"$STATE_LOG\" \"$LEGACY_LOG\"\n341\t          open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n342\t          replay_command: |\n343\t            GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n344\t            [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n345\t            RUN_DIR=\"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\"\n346\t            node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" replay-legacy-review \"$GATEWAY\" \"$RUN_DIR/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\" \"$RUN_DIR\"\n347\t        on_completed_session:\n348\t          before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n349\t          log: \"Prior session already completed. Either archive the completed review/ tree and start a fresh session, or jump straight to synthesis with the existing artifacts.\"\n350\t          skip_to: phase_synthesis\n351\t        on_invalid_state:\n352\t          halt: true\n353\t          release_lock: step_release_lock\n354\t          message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n355\t        on_fresh:\n356\t          action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n357\t\n358\t      step_scope_discovery:\n359\t        action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n360\t        resolve:\n361\t          spec-folder: |\n362\t            1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, acceptance-criteria.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n363\t            2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n364\t            3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n365\t            4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n366\t            5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n367\t            6. Set scope = the packet's own canonical docs plus all discovered implementation and test files\n368\t          skill: |\n369\t            1. Read SKILL.md from .skilled/skills/{skill_name}/\n370\t            2. Discover references/, assets/, scripts/ contents\n371\t            3. Find agent definitions referencing this skill across runtimes\n372\t            4. Find command entry points referencing this skill\n373\t            5. Set scope = all discovered files\n374\t          agent: |\n375\t            1. Find agent definition across repo-managed runtimes (.claude/agents/, .skilled/agents/)\n376\t            2. Compare agent definitions for consistency\n377\t            3. Set scope = all discovered agent files\n378\t          track: |\n379\t            1. List all child spec folders under specs/{track}/ or .opencode/specs/{track}/\n380\t            2. For each: read spec.md + acceptance-criteria.md\n381\t            3. Set scope = all child spec artifacts\n382\t          files: |\n383\t            1. Expand glob patterns from review_target\n384\t            2. Validate all files exist\n385\t            3. Discover immediate cross-references (imports, links)\n386\t            4. Set scope = expanded file list + cross-references\n387\t        outputs:\n388\t          - review_scope_files: \"List of all files in review scope\"\n389\t          - cross_reference_targets: \"{ spec_paths: [...], code_paths: [...], test_paths: [...] }\"\n390\t\n391\t      step_order_dimensions:\n392\t        action: \"Order review dimensions based on risk priority\"\n393\t        algorithm: |\n394\t          1. Iteration 0 (inventory pass): Build artifact map, identify file types, estimate complexity\n395\t          2. Subsequent iterations follow risk-ordered deep passes:\n396\t             correctness → security → traceability → maintainability\n397\t          3. If review_dimensions != \"all\", filter to only requested dimensions; each configured custom dimension follows the canonical four, in configured order\n398\t          4. Derive traceability protocol plan:\n399\t             - core: spec_code, checklist_evidence\n400\t             - overlay: skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability\n401\t          5. If resource_map_present, reserve at least one traceability-oriented pass to cross-check target_files from applied/T-*.md against resource-map.md and classify touched / expected-by-scope / gap / absent-from-map outcomes\n402\t          6. Store ordered list as dimension_queue\n403\t        outputs:\n404\t          - dimension_queue: \"Ordered list of dimensions to review\"\n405\t          - inventory_pass: true\n406\t\n407\t      step_normalize_review_dimensions:\n408\t        action: \"Normalize reviewDimensions once during init for config + JSONL reuse\"\n409\t        outputs:\n410\t          - review_dimensions_normalized: \"Canonical string[] for deep-review-config.json\"\n411\t          - review_dimensions_json: \"JSON.stringify(review_dimensions_normalized) for JSONL config record\"\n412\t          - review_dimensions_list: \"The canonical four in risk order, then each configured custom dimension in configured order, joined by ', '\"\n413\t          - dimension_coverage_custom_seed: \"For each configured custom dimension in configured order, the text ,\\\"<name>\\\":false; empty when every configured dimension is canonical\"\n414\t        normalize: |\n415\t          Accept {review_dimensions} in any of these shapes and convert once:\n416\t            - \"all\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\",\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"]\n417\t            - \"correctness,security\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\"]\n418\t            - [\"correctness\"] → [\"correctness\"]\n419\t            - \"correctness,performance\" → [\"correctness\",\"performance\"]\n420\t          Trim and lowercase each element and drop duplicates; an empty name fails setup. A name outside the four canonical dimension names is a custom dimension, kept in configured order after the canonical ones.\n421\t\n422\t      step_normalize_review_focus:\n423\t        action: \"Normalize the optional operator review focus once during init\"\n424\t        outputs:\n425\t          - review_focus_normalized: \"Single-line focus text, or empty string when no focus was given\"\n426\t        normalize: |\n427\t          Collapse every control character (C0, C1, DEL, U+2028, U+2029) and whitespace run to one space, trim, treat an empty result as absent, and fail setup when more than 1000 characters remain.\n428\t          fanout-run.cjs applies the same rule in code, so a fan-out lineage receives the same text.\n429\t\n430\t      step_resolve_session_id:\n431\t        action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve timestamp fallback\"\n432\t        branch_on: \"session_id\"\n433\t        if_present:\n434\t          bind:\n435\t            session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n436\t        if_absent:\n437\t          bind:\n438\t            session_id_init: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n439\t\n440\t      step_create_config:\n441\t        action: \"Create deep-review-config.json from template with review-specific fields\"\n442\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n443\t        template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n444\t        lineage_values:\n445\t          generation_init: \"{prior_generation + 1} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else 1\"\n446\t          lineage_mode_init: \"restart when lineage_mode == 'restart', else new\"\n447\t          parent_session_id_init: \"{prior_session_id} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else null\"\n448\t        populate:\n449\t          topic: \"Review: {review_target}\"\n450\t          mode: \"review\"\n451\t          sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n452\t          parentSessionId: \"{parent_session_id_init}\"\n453\t          lineageMode: \"{lineage_mode_init}\"\n454\t          generation: \"{generation_init}\"\n455\t          continuedFromRun: null\n456\t          reviewTarget: \"{review_target}\"\n457\t          reviewTargetType: \"{review_target_type}\"\n458\t          # Reuse the single normalized init-time value from step_normalize_review_dimensions.\n459\t          reviewDimensions: \"{review_dimensions_normalized}\"\n460\t          # Null when review_focus_normalized is empty. The review report reads it back to show the focus.\n461\t          reviewFocus: \"{review_focus_normalized}\"\n462\t          resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n463\t          reviewScopeFiles: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n464\t          severityThreshold: \"P2\"\n465\t          crossReference:\n466\t            core: [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"]\n467\t            overlay: [\"skill_agent\", \"agent_cross_runtime\", \"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n468\t          maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n469\t          # Semantic: weighted P0/P1/P2 severity ratio. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n470\t          convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n471\t          antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n472\t          antiConvergence.depthMode: \"{depth_mode}\"\n473\t          # Written as a JSON integer: frontier-admit.cjs reads a quoted number as unset and falls back to the default.\n474\t          expansiveDepth.maxDepth: \"{frontier_max_depth} when bound, else 3\"\n475\t          expansiveDepth.maxChildrenPerNode: 6\n476\t          expansiveDepth.budgetSplit: { depth1: 0.5, depth2: 0.35, depth3: 0.15 }\n477\t          # Null derives the run-wide node cap at admission as half the iteration budget, so the frontier cannot claim every iteration; the depth-1 seed answers only to the root-children cap but counts toward this one. A defaulted budget is resized from the seed by step_frontier_budget so the cap keeps room past depth 1; an explicit budget is kept as given and may leave none.\n478\t          expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes: \"{frontier_max_nodes} when bound, else null\"\n479\t          antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n480\t          stopPolicy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n481\t          stuckThreshold: 2\n482\t          maxDurationMinutes: 120\n483\t          specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n484\t          # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-review.md:71 (default true; false when flag is set).\n485\t          # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n486\t          resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n487\t          createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n488\t          status: \"initialized\"\n489\t          releaseReadinessState: \"in-progress\"\n490\t          executionMode: \"{execution_mode}\"\n491\t        output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n492\t\n493\t      step_frontier_scope:\n494\t        description: \"Record the files a commit-range target touches before admission reads them\"\n495\t        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n496\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n497\t        note: |\n498\t          Relevance and the terminal scope gate read reviewScopeFiles, and for a\n499\t          commit-range target only git knows those files. The command replaces the\n500\t          list step_scope_discovery recorded with git diff --name-only <range> --\n501\t          <pathspec>, the pathspec being the paths after '--' up to a parenthesized\n502\t          label, and leaves any other target untouched. A fan-out lineage runs it\n503\t          too, after its own step_create_config, so its list is the same as every\n504\t          other lineage's. A default-mode run never reaches this step.\n505\t        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs scope --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n506\t        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n507\t        outputs:\n508\t          - frontier_scope_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: touchedFiles, range and pathspec, or skipped\"\n509\t        on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. Admission must not run against a guessed file list.\"\n510\t\n511\t      step_frontier_seed:\n512\t        description: \"Seed the depth-1 review frontier so iteration 1 already has open nodes\"\n513\t        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n514\t        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n515\t        skip_reason: \"A fan-out lineage receives its share of the parent's seeded nodes from fanout-run.cjs; seeding again would duplicate them.\"\n516\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n517\t        instructions: |\n518\t          Decompose {review_target} and write {artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\n519\t          exactly as the root step_frontier_seed describes, then run the command.\n520\t          The decomposition is defined once, there; this call site exists because\n521\t          a fan-out run seeds before phase_init and a single-executor run seeds\n522\t          only once its config exists.\n523\t        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration 0 --input \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\" --max-iterations-source \"{max_iterations_source}\"'\n524\t        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n525\t        outputs:\n526\t          - frontier_seed_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n527\t        on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. A run that asked for expansive depth must not start without its seeded frontier.\"\n528\t\n529\t      step_frontier_budget:\n530\t        description: \"Size a defaulted expansive budget from the seed before the loop reads max_iterations\"\n531\t        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive' and max_iterations_source == 'default'\"\n532\t        skip_when: \"extension_pending == true or config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n533\t        skip_reason: \"An explicit budget always wins, an extension already set its own budget, and a fan-out lineage gets its budget from fanout-run.cjs.\"\n534\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n535\t        note: |\n536\t          The seed decides how many nodes the frontier starts with, so a defaulted budget\n537\t          is sized only now: min(24, max(loop default, 2 x c x (seeded nodes + maxDepth - 1))),\n538\t          where c is 1 for research and, for review, the four canonical dimensions less\n539\t          traceability when the configured reviewDimensions list leaves it out, plus any\n540\t          custom name, each counted once. With no seeded node, every seed pruned,\n541\t          the budget stays at the loop default. The node cap stays half the final budget.\n542\t          A default-mode run never reaches this step, so its config gains no key.\n543\t        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs budget --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n544\t        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n545\t        outputs:\n546\t          - max_iterations: \"derivedMaxIterations from the JSON output; it replaces the command default so the loop cap, the strategy and the convergence script read the same ceiling\"\n547\t          - frontier_growth_slots: \"growthSlots from the JSON output\"\n548\t        on_success: \"Print 'Expansive budget: <derivedMaxIterations> iterations, <growthSlots> growth slots past depth 1', and print the warning when the output carries one.\"\n549\t        on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. The config keeps the defaulted budget.\"\n550\t\n551\t      step_create_state_log:\n552\t        action: \"Open the run in the ledger: record deep_review.run_initialized through the append gateway, which writes the state log's first row\"\n553\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n554\t        note: |\n555\t          The state log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger, so this step never writes\n556\t          it directly. A config row written beside the ledger carries keys the projection cannot\n557\t          rebuild, and the projection refuses to drop them, so every later append in the run would\n558\t          commit to the ledger and then exit 2. Recording the run's opening as a ledger event makes\n559\t          the projected config row the state log's first row from the start. The full config stays\n560\t          in deep-review-config.json, which is what the reducer reads.\n561\t        command: |\n562\t          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n563\t          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n564\t          EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n565\t          node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" run-open-review \"{state_paths.config}\" \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n566\t          node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n567\t          STATUS=$?\n568\t          rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n569\t          exit \"$STATUS\"\n570\t        output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n571\t\n572\t      step_record_restarted_run:\n573\t        skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n574\t        action: \"Record the restarted lineage after the run-open row so the restart marker never precedes deep_review.run_initialized\"\n575\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n576\t        append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n577\t\n578\t      step_create_findings_registry:\n579\t        action: \"Initialize reducer-owned review findings registry\"\n580\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n581\t        content: '{\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"generation\":{generation_init},\"lineageMode\":\"{lineage_mode_init}\",\"openFindings\":[],\"resolvedFindings\":[],\"repeatedFindings\":[],\"dimensionCoverage\":{\"correctness\":false,\"security\":false,\"traceability\":false,\"maintainability\":false{dimension_coverage_custom_seed}},\"findingsBySeverity\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"openFindingsCount\":0,\"resolvedFindingsCount\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0.0}'\n582\t        output: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n583\t\n584\t      step_create_strategy:\n585\t        action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n586\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n587\t        template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n588\t        populate:\n589\t          review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n590\t          review_target_type: \"{review_target_type}\"\n591\t          dimensions: \"{dimension_queue}\"\n592\t          scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n593\t          cross_reference_targets: \"{cross_reference_targets}\"\n594\t          max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n595\t          convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n596\t          stop_policy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n597\t        output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n598\t\n599\t      step_seed_coverage_graph:\n600\t        action: \"Seed the review coverage graph before the first convergence check\"\n601\t        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n602\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n603\t        transform: |\n604\t          1. Convert review_scope_files into FILE nodes.\n605\t          2. Convert review target groupings into coarse SLICE nodes only; do not expand SYMBOL\n606\t             or DEPENDENCY nodes in review mode.\n607\t          3. Emit COVERS edges from SLICE nodes to FILE nodes when the grouping is known.\n608\t          4. Bind coverage_seed_source to \"scope_discovery\" and coverage_seed_confidence to 0.50.\n609\t          5. When scope discovery yields no files, emit [] for both arrays; the upsert script\n610\t             returns a warning and review continues with an empty graph.\n611\t        bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{config.sessionId}\\\" --nodes '{coverage_seed_nodes_json}' --edges '{coverage_seed_edges_json}' --seed-source \\\"{coverage_seed_source}\\\" --seed-confidence \\\"{coverage_seed_confidence}\\\"\"\n612\t        outputs:\n613\t          - coverage_seed_nodes_json: \"Seed nodes for review SLICE and FILE kinds only\"\n614\t          - coverage_seed_edges_json: \"Seed COVERS edges where review target groupings resolved\"\n615\t          - coverage_seed_warning: \"Warning emitted when the seed batch inserts zero nodes, else empty\"\n616\t        on_warning:\n617\t          log: \"Coverage graph seed inserted zero nodes; continuing with an empty graph.\"\n618\t          proceed: true\n619\t\n620\t      step_enrich_strategy_context:\n621\t        action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n622\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n623\t        condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n624\t        edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n625\t        note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n626\t\n627\t      step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n628\t        action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n629\t        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n630\t        edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n631\t        note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot and add Resource Map Coverage to the Review Charter. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n632\t\n633\t      step_frontier_reduce_seed:\n634\t        action: \"Reduce once after the seed so iteration 1 already reviews a frontier node\"\n635\t        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n636\t        dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n637\t        note: \"The loop binds active_frontier_node and the frontier dimension from registry.frontier, and step_create_findings_registry writes a registry with no frontier after the seed has run. Only the reducer projects the seeded nodes into it. Without this pass the first iteration has no frontier node and no frontier block. A fan-out lineage runs it too: its reducer_artifact_arg points the reducer at the lineage's own directory, where fanout-run.cjs put its share of the nodes.\"\n638\t        command: |\n639\t          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\n640\t        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n641\t        on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue; iteration 1 then runs on the strategy's own dimension queue and step_reduce_review_state picks the frontier up after it.\"\n642\t\n643\t      step_init_complete:\n644\t        log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created. Review scope: {review_scope_files_count} files, {dimension_queue_count} dimensions.\"\n645\t        set: { current_iteration: 1, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }\n646\t\n647\t      # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Init ───\n648\t      gate_init_approval:\n649\t        applies_to: confirm\n650\t        type: approval_gate\n651\t        purpose: \"Show review scope, dimensions, and target files. Get approval to start loop.\"\n652\t        present: |\n653\t          ## Review Initialization Complete\n654\t\n655\t          **Review Target**: {review_target} ({review_target_type})\n656\t          **Scope**: {review_scope_files_count} files\n657\t          **Dimensions**: {dimension_queue}\n658\t          **Max Iterations**: {max_iterations}\n659\t          **Convergence Threshold**: {convergence_threshold}\n660\t          **Known Context Summary**: {prior_context_summary}\n661\t\n662\t          **Files in scope:**\n663\t          {review_scope_files_summary}\n664\t\n665\t          Review `{state_paths.strategy}` for the full scope and dimension ordering.\n666\t          **State files located in**: {state_paths.packet_dir}/\n667\t\n668\t          Options:\n669\t          A) Start review loop\n670\t          B) Adjust scope or dimensions\n671\t          C) Cancel\n672\t        wait_for: \"User response\"\n673\t        after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n674\t        on_A: { set: { current_iteration: 1, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }, proceed_to: phase_loop }\n675\t        on_B: { action: \"Apply user adjustments to strategy.md, scope, or dimensions\", return_to: gate_init_approval }\n676\t        on_C: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n677\t\n678\t  # ════════\n679\t  # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n680\t  # ════════\n681\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"50357e44-6b37-4482-a890-a9dcc87cb23c","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:06:17.836Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/.claude-account2/projects/-Users-michelkerkmeester-worktrees-public-455-expansive-depth-integration/bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410/tool-results/bnb22qcnw.txt","content":"# ────────\nstate_write_protocol:\n  mechanism: \"append-gateway\"\n  command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode review --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n  applies_to: \"every append_to_jsonl and append_jsonl directive in this workflow\"\n  refusal_handling: \"halt on exit 2; never fall back to a direct file write. Exit 1 on a row that is still routed through the gateway is a workflow defect and halts; the pinned_bookkeeping rows are recorded through bookkeeping_log and are never routed.\"\n  pinned_bookkeeping:\n    events: [config_warning, lock_released, pivot_confirm_accepted, manualStop, pivot_override_accepted, maxDurationReached]\n    directive: \"bookkeeping_log\"\n    handling: \"These rows are workflow bookkeeping that the review ledger schema pins to the legacy path: they have no lossless review-event target, so the gateway would refuse them with exit 1 and write nothing. They are never sent to the gateway. The step prints the row in its log line and continues; none of them is a halt condition.\"\n  contract: |\n    The directives below specify WHAT to record; this block specifies the mechanism. The gateway\n    authorizes the write against the mode's durable authority record, serialises it behind the\n    ledger fence, returns a receipt, and refreshes state_log from the ledger. Exit 0 means the\n    record is durable in the ledger and the refreshed state_log carries it. Exit 2 means it was\n    refused, and the refusal names the check that failed.\n\n    Writing state_log directly bypasses ordering, authorization, and the receipt. Two writers\n    can then interleave with no shared ordering, and a record nobody authorized carries no\n    receipt, so a later reader cannot tell an accepted record from an invented one. A refusal\n    is a halt, never a reason to write the file directly.\n\n    There is no direct-append exception. state_log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from\n    the ledger, so a row written beside it is dropped by the next refresh: the migration\n    marker, the recovery baseline, the iteration-error row and the claim-adjudication gate\n    row are canonical ledger events like every other record.\n\nstate_paths:\n  # Template paths document the canonical packet layout. Runtime resolution happens via\n  # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep\n  # root-local review/ and child phases keep local review/ packet dirs.\n  # Canonical root-spec write targets remain review/deep-review-config.json,\n  # review/deep-review-state.jsonl, and review/deep-review-findings-registry.json.\n  packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n  local_packet_dir: \"{spec_folder}/review\"\n  legacy_root_report: \"{spec_folder}/review-report.md\"\n  config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-config.json\"\n  state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n  findings_registry: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"\n  strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n  dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n  pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review-pause\"\n  lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-review.lock\"\n  prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n  iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n  iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n  # Per-iteration structured delta stream — complement to the canonical state_log\n  # append. MUST contain at least one record with `type === \"iteration\"`; variants\n  # like `\"iteration_delta\"` are silently dropped by the reducer.\n  delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n  delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n  review_output: \"{artifact_dir}/review-report.md\"\n  resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n  archive_root: \"{artifact_archive_root}\"\n\n# ────────\n# WORKFLOW\n# ────────\n\ngate_defaults:\n  after_gate_refresh_lock:\n    action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat immediately after the operator response\"\n    command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n    on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet, so run step_release_lock and stop rather than continue without it.\"\n\nworkflow:\n\n  step_resolve_artifact_root:\n    description: \"Resolve artifact directory — use fan-out lineage override when provided, else resolve from spec_folder\"\n    note: \"Root specs keep review artifacts directly in {spec_folder}/review/. Child phases and sub-phases keep local packet directories in {spec_folder}/review/{packet}/, and archives stay local at {spec_folder}/review-archive/{packet}/.\"\n    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n    if_present:\n      bind:\n        artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n        artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n        artifact_subfolder: null\n        artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n    if_absent:\n      command: \"node -e \\\"const { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/review-research-paths.cjs'); console.log(JSON.stringify(resolveArtifactRoot('{spec_folder}', 'review')));\\\"\"\n      outputs:\n        - artifact_root_dir: \"Resolved local review owner directory\"\n        - artifact_subfolder: \"Local packet subfolder ({ownerSlug}-pt-{NN}), else null\"\n        - artifact_dir: \"Resolved review packet directory for this target\"\n        - artifact_archive_root: \"Resolved local review archive directory for this target\"\n\n  step_bind_reducer_artifact_arg:\n    description: \"Keep the reducer on the lineage-owned artifact directory during fan-out\"\n    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n    if_present:\n      bind:\n        reducer_artifact_arg: \"--artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\"\n    if_absent:\n      bind:\n        reducer_artifact_arg: \"\"\n\n  step_bind_convergence_write_arg:\n    description: \"Keep the convergence step from writing on a dry run\"\n    note: \"step_graph_convergence runs on a dry run as a preview. A live run passes --record-blocked-stop, which makes convergence.cjs append a real row on a BLOCKED decision. A dry run writes nothing, so it passes --read-only instead, which also keeps the script from persisting the graph snapshot or appending its observability event.\"\n    branch_on: \"dry_run == true\"\n    if_dry_run:\n      bind:\n        convergence_write_arg: \"--read-only\"\n    if_live_run:\n      bind:\n        convergence_write_arg: \"--record-blocked-stop\"\n\n  phase_init:\n    purpose: Create all state files for the review session and resolve review scope\n    steps:\n\n      step_preflight_contract:\n        action: \"Validate required setup bindings and executable workflow contract before any file writes\"\n        verify:\n          - required_values_present: [review_target, review_target_type, review_dimensions, spec_folder, lineage_mode, max_iterations, convergence_threshold, convergence_mode, depth_mode, stop_policy]\n          - dry_run_normalized: \"Boolean true or false before workflow loading; absent flag resolves to false.\"\n          - spec_folder_is_within: \"specs/ or .opencode/specs/ (canonicalize alias roots before validation)\"\n          - unresolved_placeholders: \"FAIL if any user-facing template references placeholders not produced by earlier steps\"\n          - tool_contract: \"FAIL if executable steps reference tools outside the command allowlist\"\n          - extend_values: \"When extend is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), and extend_minutes when bound likewise. extend_minutes without extend, or extend with a lineage_mode other than auto or completed-continue, is a usage error. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock, with a usage error that names the flag.\"\n          - frontier_cap_values: \"When frontier_max_depth or frontier_max_nodes is bound it must be a positive integer (digits only, no sign, at least 1), else fail with 'Usage error (frontier-cap-value): --frontier-max-depth needs a positive integer' or the same for --frontier-max-nodes. Either one bound while depth_mode != 'expansive' fails with 'Usage error (frontier-cap-without-expansive): --frontier-max-depth only applies with --depth-mode=expansive' or the same for --frontier-max-nodes. Each fails here, before step_acquire_lock.\"\n        on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL and report the missing binding or unsupported contract reference\"\n\n      step_create_directories:\n        action: \"Create spec folder and canonical review packet directories if they don't exist\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.prompt_dir} {state_paths.iteration_dir} {state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n\n      step_detect_resource_map:\n        action: \"Detect resource-map.md before config creation so init can persist coverage-gate state\"\n        inspect:\n          - \"{spec_folder}/resource-map.md\"\n        classify:\n          present: \"resource-map.md exists at init\"\n          absent: \"resource-map.md does not exist at init\"\n        outputs:\n          - resource_map_present: \"Boolean true when {spec_folder}/resource-map.md exists, else false\"\n          - resource_map_known_context: \"When present: concise resource-map snapshot for Known Context and charter framing. When absent: 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n\n      step_migrate_legacy_review_state:\n        action: \"Rehome legacy review artifacts into review/iterations before session classification\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        detect:\n          canonical_review_state:\n            - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n            - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n            - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n            - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n          legacy_review_state:\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md\"\n            - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause\"\n            - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n            - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report}\"\n          legacy_review_markers:\n            - \"scratch/deep-review-strategy.md exists\"\n            - \"scratch/deep-research-config.json declares mode == 'review' OR scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl contains mode == 'review'\"\n        migrate_only:\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json -> {state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl -> {state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md -> {state_paths.strategy}\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md -> {state_paths.dashboard}\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n          - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause -> {state_paths.pause_sentinel}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n          - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report} -> {state_paths.review_output}\"\n        on_canonical_present: \"Leave canonical review/ state untouched and do not overwrite it with legacy scratch artifacts.\"\n        on_legacy_detected: \"Move only the review-specific whitelist, print LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED and leave unrelated scratch files untouched. Nothing is appended here: an append before session classification would create the state log and turn a fresh packet into a partial one, and the moved state log was written without the ledger, so the gateway refuses every append to it until step_classify_session.on_moved_legacy_state adopts it.\"\n        on_conflict: \"If canonical review/ state and legacy scratch review state both exist but disagree, halt for operator repair instead of merging contradictory state.\"\n        outputs:\n          - legacy_migration_detected: \"true when the command printed LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED, else false\"\n          - migration_recorded: \"false; step_record_artifact_migration sets it once the migration row is appended\"\n        command: |\n          mkdir -p {state_paths.iteration_dir}\n          if [ ! -e {state_paths.config} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.state_log} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.strategy} ] && [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && ( [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] || [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] ); then\n            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json {state_paths.config}\n            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl {state_paths.state_log}\n            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md {state_paths.strategy}\n            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md {state_paths.dashboard}\n            find {spec_folder}/scratch -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\;\n            [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause {state_paths.pause_sentinel}\n            [ -e {state_paths.legacy_root_report} ] && mv {state_paths.legacy_root_report} {state_paths.review_output}\n            echo \"LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED\"\n          fi\n          find {state_paths.local_packet_dir} -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\; 2>/dev/null || true\n\n      step_acquire_lock:\n        action: \"Acquire the single-writer advisory lock before session classification\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        ttl_ms: \"lock_ttl_ms = max(1800000, executor_timeout * 1000). executor_timeout is the bound dispatch timeout in seconds, 900 when unset. The lock is stale after twice this value, so it outlives the longest allowed dispatch.\"\n        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs acquire --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --packet-id {spec_folder} --ttl-ms {lock_ttl_ms}\"\n        on_acquire: \"Capture lock.ownerPid as captured_owner_pid and lock.acquireNonce as captured_acquire_nonce from the JSON output, and reuse both for every release below. If acquired=false, fail closed — another deep-review run already holds this packet. Under confirm, mode_overrides.confirm.lock_not_acquired applies instead.\"\n        note: \"Uses the promoted runtime/ loop-lock CLI (single source of truth: stale-lock reclaim, clean owner-scoped release). macOS/BSD locking is advisory — best-effort single-writer, not a hard mutex across host calls. Acquire reclaims a stale lock itself and reports the old holder under `reclaimed`. A lock is stale when its heartbeat is older than twice its TTL, or when its owning process is known to be dead. No confirmation step exists in either mode: log a `reclaimed` holder and continue.\"\n        # Lock-cleanup contract: the lock file MUST be released on every terminal exit path that follows acquisition.\n        # Runtimes honoring step_acquire_lock are required to perform this cleanup before halting or pausing.\n        on_halt:\n          action: \"Every terminal halt after the acquire runs step_release_lock before it returns control\"\n          command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; failures here are logged but do not block the halt\"\n        on_cancel:\n          action: \"Release the lock on user cancel or pause-sentinel detection before sentinel processing\"\n          command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; cancel completes regardless of cleanup result\"\n        on_workflow_exit:\n          action: \"Release the lock as the final step of any workflow exit path (success or failure)\"\n          command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; idempotent — safe to invoke when already released\"\n\n      step_extend_completed_run:\n        action: \"Extend a completed run in place, under the lock and before classification, so the classifier sees a resumable run\"\n        skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'completed-continue'\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        note: |\n          --extend=N continues a finished run in the same session and generation. The\n          duration clock counts wall-clock time since createdAt, idle time included, so the\n          new budget starts from whichever is later, the old budget or the time already\n          spent, and createdAt is never re-stamped. The event is appended before the\n          config is replaced, so a failed append leaves the run complete and untouched.\n        command: |\n          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          WORK_DIR=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-extend.XXXXXX\")\"\n          node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" extend-review \"{state_paths.config}\" \"{state_paths.state_log}\" \"{extend}\" \"{extend_minutes}\" \"$WORK_DIR\" > \"$WORK_DIR/result.json\" || { STATUS=$?; rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"; exit \"$STATUS\"; }\n          node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$WORK_DIR/event.json\" || { rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"; exit 1; }\n          mv \"$WORK_DIR/config.json\" \"{state_paths.config}\" || { rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"; exit 1; }\n          cat \"$WORK_DIR/result.json\"\n          rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"\n        outputs:\n          - continued_from_run: \"continuedFromRun from the JSON output\"\n          - max_iterations: \"newMaxIterations from the JSON output; it replaces the command default so the loop cap and the convergence script read the same ceiling\"\n          - extension_pending: \"true\"\n          - extension_warning: \"warning from the JSON output, null when none\"\n        on_warning: \"When extension_warning is not null, print it and continue. It never refuses the extension.\"\n        on_fail: \"Exit 2 is a usage error, such as a run that is not complete: halt with that message through step_release_lock and leave the config untouched. Any other failure halts with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock.\"\n\n      step_snapshot_extended_review_report:\n        action: \"Keep the prior review report before the extension's first dispatch, so re-synthesis cannot overwrite it\"\n        skip_when: \"extension_pending != true\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        command: |\n          GENERATION=\"$(node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/workflow-steps.cjs generation \"{state_paths.config}\")\" || exit 1\n          SNAPSHOT=\"{state_paths.packet_dir}/review-report-v${GENERATION}-r{continued_from_run}.md\"\n          if [ -e \"$SNAPSHOT\" ]; then\n            echo \"The review report snapshot $SNAPSHOT is already there.\" >&2\n            exit 1\n          fi\n          if [ -f \"{state_paths.review_output}\" ]; then\n            cp \"{state_paths.review_output}\" \"$SNAPSHOT\"\n          fi\n        note: \"Keyed by generation and continuedFromRun, so a second extension of the same generation writes its own snapshot.\"\n        on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. Never overwrite an existing snapshot.\"\n\n      step_classify_session:\n        action: \"Classify the session before writing files\"\n        inspect:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        classify:\n          fresh: \"None of the three state artifacts exist\"\n          resume: \"Config, JSONL, and strategy all exist and config.mode == 'review' and agree on target/spec folder\"\n          completed-session: \"Resume artifacts exist and config.status == 'complete'\"\n          invalid-state: \"Any partial, missing, or contradictory combination\"\n        extension_rule: \"When extension_pending == true, step_extend_completed_run has just set status initialized and appended run_extended, so a synthesis_complete row followed by an extended row is consistent: classify as resume, never as invalid-state or completed-session.\"\n        outputs:\n          - session_state: \"fresh | resume | completed-session | invalid-state\"\n          - prior_tail_digest: \"sha256 of the state log bytes when resuming or restarting an existing lineage\"\n        lifecycle_routing:\n          - \"If lineage_mode == restart, step_apply_lifecycle_request archived the packet before the lock was taken, so session_state is fresh and on_fresh runs.\"\n          - \"If lineage_mode == auto or lineage_mode == resume, preserve the existing resume/completed/fresh behavior.\"\n        on_resume:\n          before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n          log: \"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent. Continue the same lineage (sessionId unchanged, generation unchanged, no archive).\"\n          append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_resumed\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"sourceSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"resumeReason\":\"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent; continue the same lineage.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n          extension_override: \"When extension_pending == true, skip this append_jsonl: step_extend_completed_run already recorded the lifecycle action as run_extended, so the ledger carries one event per action. Keep lineage_mode completed-continue and skip_to phase_loop.\"\n          skip_to: phase_loop\n          confirm_choice:\n            applies_to: confirm\n            preempts: \"Under confirm this block runs in place of the sibling log, append_jsonl and skip_to keys of on_resume. Under auto it is skipped and those keys run.\"\n            show_dashboard: \"{state_paths.dashboard}\"\n            ask: \"Existing review session is consistent. Resume where it left off, or restart (archive the current review packet under the root-level review-archive/ tree and start a fresh session)?\"\n            after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n            options: [resume, restart, cancel]\n            on_resume_choice:\n              dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n              before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n              set:\n                lineage_mode: \"resume\"\n                parent_session_id: \"{session_id}\"\n              append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_resumed\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"sourceSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"resumeReason\":\"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent; continue the same lineage.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n              skip_to: gate_init_approval\n              extension_override: \"When extension_pending == true, do not set lineage_mode to resume and do not append the resumed row, because run_extended already records this extension. Keep lineage_mode completed-continue and skip_to gate_init_approval.\"\n            on_restart_choice:\n              dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n              bind_prior_lineage:\n                action: \"Read the session id and generation of the packet that is about to be archived\"\n                command: |\n                  node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/workflow-steps.cjs prior-lineage \"{state_paths.config}\" \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n                outputs:\n                  - prior_session_id: \"priorSessionId from the JSON output, null when no old config exists\"\n                  - prior_generation: \"priorGeneration from the JSON output, 0 when no old config exists\"\n                  - prior_tail_digest: \"priorTailDigest from the JSON output: the sha256 of the old state log bytes, or of zero bytes when no old state log exists\"\n                on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. The old config is unreadable, so repair or archive the packet by hand.\"\n              command: |\n                if [ -e \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\" ]; then\n                  echo \"The archive folder {state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug} is already there.\" >&2\n                  exit 1\n                fi\n                mkdir -p \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\" || exit 1\n                find \"{state_paths.packet_dir}\" -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 ! -name \"$(basename \"{state_paths.lock_file}\")\" -exec mv {} \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}/\" \\; || exit 1\n                mkdir -p \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}\" \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}\" \"{state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n              on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL through step_release_lock. Never fall back to resume.\"\n              set:\n                lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n              skip_to: step_create_config\n            on_cancel_choice:\n              halt: true\n              release_lock: step_release_lock\n              message: \"Review session preserved. Manually archive or edit review/ before re-running.\"\n        on_restart:\n          action: \"Nothing is archived here. step_apply_lifecycle_request archived the packet before the lock was taken, so a restart run reaches this step as fresh and continues as on_fresh.\"\n        note_deferred_branches: \"fork is deferred and not runtime-supported in this release.\"\n        note_live_branches: \"completed-continue is live through --extend=N: step_extend_completed_run reopens a completed run before classification, so it lands here as resume. The live modes are new, resume, restart and completed-continue. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches for the one-session contract.\"\n        on_moved_legacy_state:\n          applies_when: \"legacy_migration_detected == true and the branch taken resumes the session or goes to synthesis; never on restart or cancel\"\n          order: \"Runs after classification and before that branch appends anything, the resume event included.\"\n          note: |\n            The state log moved out of scratch/ was written by hand before the ledger existed, so the\n            gateway refuses every append to it. Set it aside unchanged as deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl,\n            open the run from the moved config, then replay its iteration rows through the gateway,\n            which carries each one whole. Rows the gateway cannot carry stay only in the set-aside file,\n            and the replay reports how many. Exit 2 from any of the three is a halt.\n          set_aside_command: |\n            STATE_LOG=\"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n            LEGACY_LOG=\"$(dirname \"$STATE_LOG\")/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\"\n            if [ -e \"$LEGACY_LOG\" ]; then\n              echo \"A set-aside legacy state log already exists at $LEGACY_LOG. Repair the packet by hand.\" >&2\n              exit 1\n            fi\n            mv \"$STATE_LOG\" \"$LEGACY_LOG\"\n          open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n          replay_command: |\n            GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n            [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n            RUN_DIR=\"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\"\n            node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" replay-legacy-review \"$GATEWAY\" \"$RUN_DIR/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\" \"$RUN_DIR\"\n        on_completed_session:\n          before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n          log: \"Prior session already completed. Either archive the completed review/ tree and start a fresh session, or jump straight to synthesis with the existing artifacts.\"\n          skip_to: phase_synthesis\n        on_invalid_state:\n          halt: true\n          release_lock: step_release_lock\n          message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n        on_fresh:\n          action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n\n      step_scope_discovery:\n        action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n        resolve:\n          spec-folder: |\n            1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, acceptance-criteria.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n            2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n            3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n            4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n            5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n            6. Set scope = the packet's own canonical docs plus all discovered implementation and test files\n          skill: |\n            1. Read SKILL.md from .skilled/skills/{skill_name}/\n            2. Discover references/, assets/, scripts/ contents\n            3. Find agent definitions referencing this skill across runtimes\n            4. Find command entry points referencing this skill\n            5. Set scope = all discovered files\n          agent: |\n            1. Find agent definition across repo-managed runtimes (.claude/agents/, .skilled/agents/)\n            2. Compare agent definitions for consistency\n            3. Set scope = all discovered agent files\n          track: |\n            1. List all child spec folders under specs/{track}/ or .opencode/specs/{track}/\n            2. For each: read spec.md + acceptance-criteria.md\n            3. Set scope = all child spec artifacts\n          files: |\n            1. Expand glob patterns from review_target\n            2. Validate all files exist\n            3. Discover immediate cross-references (imports, links)\n            4. Set scope = expanded file list + cross-references\n        outputs:\n          - review_scope_files: \"List of all files in review scope\"\n          - cross_reference_targets: \"{ spec_paths: [...], code_paths: [...], test_paths: [...] }\"\n\n      step_order_dimensions:\n        action: \"Order review dimensions based on risk priority\"\n        algorithm: |\n          1. Iteration 0 (inventory pass): Build artifact map, identify file types, estimate complexity\n          2. Subsequent iterations follow risk-ordered deep passes:\n             correctness → security → traceability → maintainability\n          3. If review_dimensions != \"all\", filter to only requested dimensions; each configured custom dimension follows the canonical four, in configured order\n          4. Derive traceability protocol plan:\n             - core: spec_code, checklist_evidence\n             - overlay: skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability\n          5. If resource_map_present, reserve at least one traceability-oriented pass to cross-check target_files from applied/T-*.md against resource-map.md and classify touched / expected-by-scope / gap / absent-from-map outcomes\n          6. Store ordered list as dimension_queue\n        outputs:\n          - dimension_queue: \"Ordered list of dimensions to review\"\n          - inventory_pass: true\n\n      step_normalize_review_dimensions:\n        action: \"Normalize reviewDimensions once during init for config + JSONL reuse\"\n        outputs:\n          - review_dimensions_normalized: \"Canonical string[] for deep-review-config.json\"\n          - review_dimensions_json: \"JSON.stringify(review_dimensions_normalized) for JSONL config record\"\n          - review_dimensions_list: \"The canonical four in risk order, then each configured custom dimension in configured order, joined by ', '\"\n          - dimension_coverage_custom_seed: \"For each configured custom dimension in configured order, the text ,\\\"<name>\\\":false; empty when every configured dimension is canonical\"\n        normalize: |\n          Accept {review_dimensions} in any of these shapes and convert once:\n            - \"all\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\",\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"]\n            - \"correctness,security\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\"]\n            - [\"correctness\"] → [\"correctness\"]\n            - \"correctness,performance\" → [\"correctness\",\"performance\"]\n          Trim and lowercase each element and drop duplicates; an empty name fails setup. A name outside the four canonical dimension names is a custom dimension, kept in configured order after the canonical ones.\n\n      step_normalize_review_focus:\n        action: \"Normalize the optional operator review focus once during init\"\n        outputs:\n          - review_focus_normalized: \"Single-line focus text, or empty string when no focus was given\"\n        normalize: |\n          Collapse every control character (C0, C1, DEL, U+2028, U+2029) and whitespace run to one space, trim, treat an empty result as absent, and fail setup when more than 1000 characters remain.\n          fanout-run.cjs applies the same rule in code, so a fan-out lineage receives the same text.\n\n      step_resolve_session_id:\n        action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve timestamp fallback\"\n        branch_on: \"session_id\"\n        if_present:\n          bind:\n            session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n        if_absent:\n          bind:\n            session_id_init: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n\n      step_create_config:\n        action: \"Create deep-review-config.json from template with review-specific fields\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n        lineage_values:\n          generation_init: \"{prior_generation + 1} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else 1\"\n          lineage_mode_init: \"restart when lineage_mode == 'restart', else new\"\n          parent_session_id_init: \"{prior_session_id} when lineage_mode == 'restart', else null\"\n        populate:\n          topic: \"Review: {review_target}\"\n          mode: \"review\"\n          sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n          parentSessionId: \"{parent_session_id_init}\"\n          lineageMode: \"{lineage_mode_init}\"\n          generation: \"{generation_init}\"\n          continuedFromRun: null\n          reviewTarget: \"{review_target}\"\n          reviewTargetType: \"{review_target_type}\"\n          # Reuse the single normalized init-time value from step_normalize_review_dimensions.\n          reviewDimensions: \"{review_dimensions_normalized}\"\n          # Null when review_focus_normalized is empty. The review report reads it back to show the focus.\n          reviewFocus: \"{review_focus_normalized}\"\n          resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n          reviewScopeFiles: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n          severityThreshold: \"P2\"\n          crossReference:\n            core: [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"]\n            overlay: [\"skill_agent\", \"agent_cross_runtime\", \"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n          maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n          # Semantic: weighted P0/P1/P2 severity ratio. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n          convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n          antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n          antiConvergence.depthMode: \"{depth_mode}\"\n          # Written as a JSON integer: frontier-admit.cjs reads a quoted number as unset and falls back to the default.\n          expansiveDepth.maxDepth: \"{frontier_max_depth} when bound, else 3\"\n          expansiveDepth.maxChildrenPerNode: 6\n          expansiveDepth.budgetSplit: { depth1: 0.5, depth2: 0.35, depth3: 0.15 }\n          # Null derives the run-wide node cap at admission as half the iteration budget, so the frontier cannot claim every iteration; the depth-1 seed answers only to the root-children cap but counts toward this one. A defaulted budget is resized from the seed by step_frontier_budget so the cap keeps room past depth 1; an explicit budget is kept as given and may leave none.\n          expansiveDepth.maxFrontierNodes: \"{frontier_max_nodes} when bound, else null\"\n          antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n          stopPolicy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n          stuckThreshold: 2\n          maxDurationMinutes: 120\n          specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n          # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-review.md:71 (default true; false when flag is set).\n          # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n          resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n          createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n          status: \"initialized\"\n          releaseReadinessState: \"in-progress\"\n          executionMode: \"{execution_mode}\"\n        output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n\n      step_frontier_scope:\n        description: \"Record the files a commit-range target touches before admission reads them\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        note: |\n          Relevance and the terminal scope gate read reviewScopeFiles, and for a\n          commit-range target only git knows those files. The command replaces the\n          list step_scope_discovery recorded with git diff --name-only <range> --\n          <pathspec>, the pathspec being the paths after '--' up to a parenthesized\n          label, and leaves any other target untouched. A fan-out lineage runs it\n          too, after its own step_create_config, so its list is the same as every\n          other lineage's. A default-mode run never reaches this step.\n        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs scope --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        outputs:\n          - frontier_scope_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: touchedFiles, range and pathspec, or skipped\"\n        on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. Admission must not run against a guessed file list.\"\n\n      step_frontier_seed:\n        description: \"Seed the depth-1 review frontier so iteration 1 already has open nodes\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n        skip_reason: \"A fan-out lineage receives its share of the parent's seeded nodes from fanout-run.cjs; seeding again would duplicate them.\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        instructions: |\n          Decompose {review_target} and write {artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\n          exactly as the root step_frontier_seed describes, then run the command.\n          The decomposition is defined once, there; this call site exists because\n          a fan-out run seeds before phase_init and a single-executor run seeds\n          only once its config exists.\n        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs seed --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration 0 --input \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-seed.json\" --max-iterations-source \"{max_iterations_source}\"'\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        outputs:\n          - frontier_seed_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n        on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. A run that asked for expansive depth must not start without its seeded frontier.\"\n\n      step_frontier_budget:\n        description: \"Size a defaulted expansive budget from the seed before the loop reads max_iterations\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive' and max_iterations_source == 'default'\"\n        skip_when: \"extension_pending == true or config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is present\"\n        skip_reason: \"An explicit budget always wins, an extension already set its own budget, and a fan-out lineage gets its budget from fanout-run.cjs.\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        note: |\n          The seed decides how many nodes the frontier starts with, so a defaulted budget\n          is sized only now: min(24, max(loop default, 2 x c x (seeded nodes + maxDepth - 1))),\n          where c is 1 for research and, for review, the four canonical dimensions less\n          traceability when the configured reviewDimensions list leaves it out, plus any\n          custom name, each counted once. With no seeded node, every seed pruned,\n          the budget stays at the loop default. The node cap stays half the final budget.\n          A default-mode run never reaches this step, so its config gains no key.\n        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs budget --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\"'\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        outputs:\n          - max_iterations: \"derivedMaxIterations from the JSON output; it replaces the command default so the loop cap, the strategy and the convergence script read the same ceiling\"\n          - frontier_growth_slots: \"growthSlots from the JSON output\"\n        on_success: \"Print 'Expansive budget: <derivedMaxIterations> iterations, <growthSlots> growth slots past depth 1', and print the warning when the output carries one.\"\n        on_failure: \"Halt with the command's stderr line. The config keeps the defaulted budget.\"\n\n      step_create_state_log:\n        action: \"Open the run in the ledger: record deep_review.run_initialized through the append gateway, which writes the state log's first row\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        note: |\n          The state log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger, so this step never writes\n          it directly. A config row written beside the ledger carries keys the projection cannot\n          rebuild, and the projection refuses to drop them, so every later append in the run would\n          commit to the ledger and then exit 2. Recording the run's opening as a ledger event makes\n          the projected config row the state log's first row from the start. The full config stays\n          in deep-review-config.json, which is what the reducer reads.\n        command: |\n          GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n          EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n          node \"$(dirname \"$GATEWAY\")/workflow-steps.cjs\" run-open-review \"{state_paths.config}\" \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n          node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n          STATUS=$?\n          rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n          exit \"$STATUS\"\n        output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n\n      step_record_restarted_run:\n        skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n        action: \"Record the restarted lineage after the run-open row so the restart marker never precedes deep_review.run_initialized\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n\n      step_create_findings_registry:\n        action: \"Initialize reducer-owned review findings registry\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        content: '{\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"generation\":{generation_init},\"lineageMode\":\"{lineage_mode_init}\",\"openFindings\":[],\"resolvedFindings\":[],\"repeatedFindings\":[],\"dimensionCoverage\":{\"correctness\":false,\"security\":false,\"traceability\":false,\"maintainability\":false{dimension_coverage_custom_seed}},\"findingsBySeverity\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"openFindingsCount\":0,\"resolvedFindingsCount\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0.0}'\n        output: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n\n      step_create_strategy:\n        action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n        populate:\n          review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n          review_target_type: \"{review_target_type}\"\n          dimensions: \"{dimension_queue}\"\n          scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n          cross_reference_targets: \"{cross_reference_targets}\"\n          max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n          convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n          stop_policy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n        output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n\n      step_seed_coverage_graph:\n        action: \"Seed the review coverage graph before the first convergence check\"\n        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        transform: |\n          1. Convert review_scope_files into FILE nodes.\n          2. Convert review target groupings into coarse SLICE nodes only; do not expand SYMBOL\n             or DEPENDENCY nodes in review mode.\n          3. Emit COVERS edges from SLICE nodes to FILE nodes when the grouping is known.\n          4. Bind coverage_seed_source to \"scope_discovery\" and coverage_seed_confidence to 0.50.\n          5. When scope discovery yields no files, emit [] for both arrays; the upsert script\n             returns a warning and review continues with an empty graph.\n        bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{config.sessionId}\\\" --nodes '{coverage_seed_nodes_json}' --edges '{coverage_seed_edges_json}' --seed-source \\\"{coverage_seed_source}\\\" --seed-confidence \\\"{coverage_seed_confidence}\\\"\"\n        outputs:\n          - coverage_seed_nodes_json: \"Seed nodes for review SLICE and FILE kinds only\"\n          - coverage_seed_edges_json: \"Seed COVERS edges where review target groupings resolved\"\n          - coverage_seed_warning: \"Warning emitted when the seed batch inserts zero nodes, else empty\"\n        on_warning:\n          log: \"Coverage graph seed inserted zero nodes; continuing with an empty graph.\"\n          proceed: true\n\n      step_enrich_strategy_context:\n        action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n        edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n\n      step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n        action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot and add Resource Map Coverage to the Review Charter. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n\n      step_frontier_reduce_seed:\n        action: \"Reduce once after the seed so iteration 1 already reviews a frontier node\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n        note: \"The loop binds active_frontier_node and the frontier dimension from registry.frontier, and step_create_findings_registry writes a registry with no frontier after the seed has run. Only the reducer projects the seeded nodes into it. Without this pass the first iteration has no frontier node and no frontier block. A fan-out lineage runs it too: its reducer_artifact_arg points the reducer at the lineage's own directory, where fanout-run.cjs put its share of the nodes.\"\n        command: |\n          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue; iteration 1 then runs on the strategy's own dimension queue and step_reduce_review_state picks the frontier up after it.\"\n\n      step_init_complete:\n        log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created. Review scope: {review_scope_files_count} files, {dimension_queue_count} dimensions.\"\n        set: { current_iteration: 1, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }\n\n      # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Init ───\n      gate_init_approval:\n        applies_to: confirm\n        type: approval_gate\n        purpose: \"Show review scope, dimensions, and target files. Get approval to start loop.\"\n        present: |\n          ## Review Initialization Complete\n\n          **Review Target**: {review_target} ({review_target_type})\n          **Scope**: {review_scope_files_count} files\n          **Dimensions**: {dimension_queue}\n          **Max Iterations**: {max_iterations}\n          **Convergence Threshold**: {convergence_threshold}\n          **Known Context Summary**: {prior_context_summary}\n\n          **Files in scope:**\n          {review_scope_files_summary}\n\n          Review `{state_paths.strategy}` for the full scope and dimension ordering.\n          **State files located in**: {state_paths.packet_dir}/\n\n          Options:\n          A) Start review loop\n          B) Adjust scope or dimensions\n          C) Cancel\n        wait_for: \"User response\"\n        after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n        on_A: { set: { current_iteration: 1, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }, proceed_to: phase_loop }\n        on_B: { action: \"Apply user adjustments to strategy.md, scope, or dimensions\", return_to: gate_init_approval }\n        on_C: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n\n  # ════════\n  # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n  # ════════\n","numLines":681,"startLine":1,"totalLines":681}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VafqANg62ZbHggE3k5AzrF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"system","subtype":"thinking_tokens","estimated_tokens":50,"estimated_tokens_delta":50,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"5db4ab67-2223-4796-b9de-ab279b44aa55"}
