{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ACNZYwscDu9jvbyvHhS2q6","type":"tool_result","content":"FRONTIER (expansive depth)\nCurrent node: F-1-001 at depth 1 of 3, scope .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/lineage-timestamp-window.ts. Review dimension for this node: correctness.\nSet this iteration record's \"focus\" to \"Frontier node F-1-001: correctness\" and add \"frontierNodeId\":\"F-1-001\" to it, so the run can tell which node this iteration worked.\nYou may append up to 6 `frontier_proposal` rows to this iteration's delta with \"parentId\":\"F-1-001\", one per sub-target your evidence opened inside this node. Each row needs \"question\" (what to review), \"scope\" (paths inside the review target) and \"evidence\". The admission step prunes duplicates, anything outside the review target, anything past the depth or fan-out caps, and any budget above one the parent recorded. Never write review/frontier-nodes.jsonl or a coverage surface yourself.\n      83\ncommit 87223d32b9268b97015285bb28215f17df4329c5\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <<redacted>>\nDate:   Fri Nov 20 15:32:31 2026 +0100\n\n    feat(system-deep-loop): judge fan-out passes and show them live\n    \n    Claude lineages ran with text output, so their cost was unknown and their tool calls were\n    uncountable. They now run with stream-json and verbose output; the cost is the last result\n    event's cumulative total, and the pending-question and quota checks read the final answer, so\n    text quoted in a tool result no longer decides them.\n    \n    passEvidence reads the runner log against the gateway commits and reports, per pass, tool calls,\n    source reads, commit gap and stamp skew. It flags a pass as unexamined when it has no reads and\n    no findings, a commit gap under 15 s with no calls, or a stamp later than its commit. Counts a log\n    cannot give stay unknown, never zero.\n    \n    Progress rows now carry iterations, the last commit time, node counts and flagged passes, read\n    live from the attempt's streamed output, and a read-only --status prints them per lineage.\n    \n    Spec: system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode\n    Commit-Id: 0015428\n\n .../runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs                 | 100 +++++++-\n .../runtime/scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs             | 269 ++++++++++++++++++++-\n .../runtime/scripts/lib/cli-guards.cjs             |  55 ++++-\n .../stress/cli-adapter/fixtures/adapter-suite.ts   |   2 +-\n .../runtime/tests/unit/combo-matrix.vitest.ts      |   2 +-\n .../tests/unit/fanout-claude-stream-json.vitest.ts | 179 ++++++++++++++\n .../tests/unit/fanout-pass-evidence.vitest.ts      | 224 +++++++++++++++++\n .../runtime/tests/unit/fanout-status.vitest.ts     | 180 ++++++++++++++\n 8 files changed, 998 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)\n\ncommit 0e49309a70147ef9d5418c5428a73fb92419018e\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <<redacted>>\nDate:   Fri Nov 20 16:00:12 2026 +0100\n\n    fix(system-deep-loop): judge a lineage's timestamp window by the claimed stamp\n    \n    Once the gateway timed iteration rows and kept the model's stamp as claimedTimestamp, the\n    fan-out timestamp-window check and the completion check read only the gateway time, so a lineage\n    that fabricated its stamps no longer raised a timestamp anomaly or a stamped-after-completion\n    failure. Both checks now judge a row's claimedTimestamp when it carries one, and its timestamp\n    otherwise.\n    \n    Spec: system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode\n    Commit-Id: 0015442\n\n .../lib/deep-loop/lineage-timestamp-window.ts      | 12 ++++++++---\n .../tests/unit/lineage-timestamp-window.vitest.ts  | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"9c41899b-c918-4fa4-b855-c0347310c09c","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:07:59.765Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"FRONTIER (expansive depth)\nCurrent node: F-1-001 at depth 1 of 3, scope .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/lineage-timestamp-window.ts. Review dimension for this node: correctness.\nSet this iteration record's \"focus\" to \"Frontier node F-1-001: correctness\" and add \"frontierNodeId\":\"F-1-001\" to it, so the run can tell which node this iteration worked.\nYou may append up to 6 `frontier_proposal` rows to this iteration's delta with \"parentId\":\"F-1-001\", one per sub-target your evidence opened inside this node. Each row needs \"question\" (what to review), \"scope\" (paths inside the review target) and \"evidence\". The admission step prunes duplicates, anything outside the review target, anything past the depth or fan-out caps, and any budget above one the parent recorded. Never write review/frontier-nodes.jsonl or a coverage surface yourself.\n      83\ncommit 87223d32b9268b97015285bb28215f17df4329c5\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <<redacted>>\nDate:   Fri Nov 20 15:32:31 2026 +0100\n\n    feat(system-deep-loop): judge fan-out passes and show them live\n    \n    Claude lineages ran with text output, so their cost was unknown and their tool calls were\n    uncountable. They now run with stream-json and verbose output; the cost is the last result\n    event's cumulative total, and the pending-question and quota checks read the final answer, so\n    text quoted in a tool result no longer decides them.\n    \n    passEvidence reads the runner log against the gateway commits and reports, per pass, tool calls,\n    source reads, commit gap and stamp skew. It flags a pass as unexamined when it has no reads and\n    no findings, a commit gap under 15 s with no calls, or a stamp later than its commit. Counts a log\n    cannot give stay unknown, never zero.\n    \n    Progress rows now carry iterations, the last commit time, node counts and flagged passes, read\n    live from the attempt's streamed output, and a read-only --status prints them per lineage.\n    \n    Spec: system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode\n    Commit-Id: 0015428\n\n .../runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs                 | 100 +++++++-\n .../runtime/scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs             | 269 ++++++++++++++++++++-\n .../runtime/scripts/lib/cli-guards.cjs             |  55 ++++-\n .../stress/cli-adapter/fixtures/adapter-suite.ts   |   2 +-\n .../runtime/tests/unit/combo-matrix.vitest.ts      |   2 +-\n .../tests/unit/fanout-claude-stream-json.vitest.ts | 179 ++++++++++++++\n .../tests/unit/fanout-pass-evidence.vitest.ts      | 224 +++++++++++++++++\n .../runtime/tests/unit/fanout-status.vitest.ts     | 180 ++++++++++++++\n 8 files changed, 998 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)\n\ncommit 0e49309a70147ef9d5418c5428a73fb92419018e\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <<redacted>>\nDate:   Fri Nov 20 16:00:12 2026 +0100\n\n    fix(system-deep-loop): judge a lineage's timestamp window by the claimed stamp\n    \n    Once the gateway timed iteration rows and kept the model's stamp as claimedTimestamp, the\n    fan-out timestamp-window check and the completion check read only the gateway time, so a lineage\n    that fabricated its stamps no longer raised a timestamp anomaly or a stamped-after-completion\n    failure. Both checks now judge a row's claimedTimestamp when it carries one, and its timestamp\n    otherwise.\n    \n    Spec: system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode\n    Commit-Id: 0015442\n\n .../lib/deep-loop/lineage-timestamp-window.ts      | 12 ++++++++---\n .../tests/unit/lineage-timestamp-window.vitest.ts  | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++\n 2 files ch