{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GsjT7EDNDaMwQjvVwchMrU","type":"tool_result","content":"      step_graph_convergence:\n        action: \"Run convergence.cjs once: it evaluates the coverage graph and computes the whole review stop decision\"\n        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n        inspect:\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n        transform: |\n          1. Call convergence.cjs once on the current review lineage. It returns the graph decision and the stop_decision object.\n          2. Record the decision as one of CONTINUE, STOP_ALLOWED, STOP_BLOCKED.\n          3. Preserve raw graph signals and blockers for reducer rollup and blocked-stop evidence.\n          4. Normalize blockers to both JSON array and CSV forms for downstream stop handling.\n          5. Set graph_stop_blocked = true only when graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\".\n        bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"review\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\" --depth-mode \"{depth_mode}\" --stop-decision --config-path \"{state_paths.config}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" --iteration-count \"{iteration_count}\" --security-sensitive-fix-scope \"{security_sensitive_fix_scope}\" --fix-replay-required-rows \"{fix_completeness_replay_required_rows}\" --fix-replay-passing-rows \"{fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" {convergence_write_arg}'\n        note: \"The script is the only place the stop decision is computed. step_check_convergence branches on its stop_decision output. On a BLOCKED decision, {convergence_write_arg} passes --record-blocked-stop on a live run, which makes the script append the deep_review.blocked_stop_recorded event for this iteration through the append gateway itself, once per iteration and blocker set, so a leaf that never reaches step_emit_blocked_stop still leaves the block in the ledger. It records on an empty graph and on a graph that cannot be read as well. The event names graph-{session_id}-g{generation}-i{current_iteration}, the graph_convergence_evaluated event this step appends after the script returns. A dry run binds {convergence_write_arg} to --read-only, so the script appends no blocked-stop row, persists no snapshot and writes no observability event.\"\n        append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.graph_convergence_evaluated\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"rawSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"weightedSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"dimensionCoverageDigest\":\"{dimension_coverage_digest}\",\"protocolCoverageDigest\":\"{protocol_coverage_digest}\",\"findingStability\":\"{finding_stability}\",\"p0p1ResolutionState\":\"{p0p1_resolution_state}\",\"evidenceDensity\":{evidence_density},\"hotspotSaturation\":{hotspot_saturation},\"decision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"policyFingerprint\":\"{policy_fingerprint}\",\"blockerIds\":{graph_blocker_ids_json},\"stopCandidate\":{stop_candidate},\"graphDecision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"graphDigest\":\"{graph_digest}\",\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json}},\"eventId\":\"graph-{session_id}-g{generation}-i{current_iteration}\"}'\n        dry_run_event_policy: preview-only\n        on_missing_counters: \"If loop_counters_json is missing from the output, halt with stop reason error. Never bind a default counter. Run step_release_lock before the halt returns control.\"\n        outputs:\n          - graph_decision: \"CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED\"\n          - stop_decision: \"Tool stop_decision object: decision, stopReason, reasonDetail, weightedStopScore, signals, gates, blockedBy, graphDecision, inputs\"\n          - loop_counters_json: \"Tool loop_counters_json object: stuckCount and consecutiveFailureCount, both rebuilt from the state log on this pass; under expansive depth stuckCount counts only the active frontier node's own iterations\"\n          - stuck_count: \"loop_counters_json.stuckCount\"\n          - consecutive_failure_count: \"loop_counters_json.consecutiveFailureCount\"\n          - graph_decision_code: \"CONTINUE maps to continue, STOP_ALLOWED to converged, STOP_BLOCKED to blocked\"\n          - graph_signals_json: \"JSON object returned by convergence.cjs\"\n          - graph_raw_signals_json: \"Exact-field convergence-signals JSON built from the convergence.cjs signals; observationDigest is the sha256 of graph_signals_json\"\n          - graph_blockers_json: \"JSON array of graph blockers when present, else []\"\n          - graph_blocker_ids_json: \"JSON array of blocker type values; use [\\\"graph_blocker\\\"] when the decision is blocked and the list is empty\"\n          - graph_blockers_csv: \"Comma-separated blocker summary when graph blocks STOP, else empty string\"\n          - graph_stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n          - dimension_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the registry dimensionCoverage map\"\n          - protocol_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the protocol coverage object in graph_signals_json, or of {} when absent\"\n          - finding_stability: \"stable when findingStabilityRatio >= convergenceThreshold, unstable when below, unknown when the signal is missing\"\n          - p0p1_resolution_state: \"resolved when active P0 + P1 findings are 0, blocked when above 0, unknown when counts are unavailable\"\n          - evidence_density: \"evidenceDensityRatio from graph_signals_json, capped at 1\"\n          - hotspot_saturation: \"hotspotSaturationRatio from graph_signals_json, between 0 and 1\"\n          - policy_fingerprint: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON {convergenceThreshold, stopPolicy, convergenceMode} from the review config\"\n          - stop_candidate: \"true when graph_decision == STOP_ALLOWED, else false\"\n          - graph_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of graph_signals_json\"\n          - blocked_stop_record: \"Present only when stop_decision.decision == BLOCKED: status recorded, already_recorded or failed, the run, the recoveryStrategy code, the recoveryHint and the gateResults rows the event carries.\"\n        on_blocked_stop_record_failed: \"When blocked_stop_record.status == failed the script exits with the gateway status after printing the decision. Treat it as a gateway refusal under state_write_protocol.refusal_handling: halt, and never write the event by hand.\"\n\n      step_check_convergence:\n        action: \"Branch on the stop decision that convergence.cjs computed in step_graph_convergence\"\n        algorithm: |\n          The whole stop decision is computed by convergence.cjs from the review config, the state log, the findings registry and the coverage graph. This step performs no arithmetic and never recomputes or overrides the result.\n          The ratio signals leave out every iteration that is not evidence-bearing (thought, error, timeout), and stuck_count is loop_counters_json.stuckCount.\n          The script applies this fixed order, first match wins:\n          1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap is evaluated before every veto, the claim-adjudication veto included; failed legal-stop gates are recorded in stop_decision.blockedBy as synthesis evidence.\n          1a. After 3 consecutive failed iterations (status error or timeout), halt the loop and enter synthesis with stop reason error and partial findings.\n          2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n          3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue.\n      step_frontier_admit:\n        action: \"Admit this iteration's review frontier_proposal rows as sub-target nodes before the reducer runs\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive'\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        instructions: |\n          The review leaf only proposes; this step decides. Before the command, write a\n          JSON array of strings to {artifact_dir}/frontier-known-texts.json holding every\n          frontier node question already in registry.frontier.nodes and every ruled-out\n          candidate rationale, so a proposal that repeats settled work is pruned as a\n          duplicate. An absent registry gives an empty array. The helper runs the six\n          admission checks in order and writes only node-store rows: a review run queues\n          its nodes from that store alone, with no separate question queue to append.\n        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs admit --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" --input \"{state_paths.delta_pattern with NNN = current_iteration}\" --known-texts \"{artifact_dir}/frontier-known-texts.json\"'\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        outputs:\n          - frontier_admit_json: \"The JSON line the command prints: admitted node ids and pruned {nodeId, reason} rows\"\n        on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue to step_reduce_review_state; a failed admission leaves the frontier as it was and never blocks the iteration.\"\n\n      step_reduce_review_state:\n        action: \"Run reducer to refresh the canonical findings registry before dashboard generation\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"reducer-refresh\"\n      step_frontier_activate:\n        description: \"Mark the active frontier node before the iteration dispatches\"\n        enabled_when: \"depth_mode == 'expansive' AND active_frontier_node is non-empty\"\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        note: \"Marking the node active at this iteration lets the reducer attribute the iteration to the node even when the leaf rewords its focus, so the node's own coverage keeps moving instead of the iteration sliding back onto the global dimension queue.\"\n        command: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/frontier-admit.cjs close --target review --artifact-dir \"{artifact_dir}\" --node-id \"{active_frontier_node}\" --status active --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        on_failure: \"Log the stderr line as a config_warning bookkeeping event and continue; the leaf's frontierNodeId and focus marker still attribute the iteration.\"\n\n      step_dispatch_iteration:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"3c55a741-724c-42bb-8e5a-cd784ff2b752","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:10:20.754Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"      step_graph_convergence:\n        action: \"Run convergence.cjs once: it evaluates the coverage graph and computes the whole review stop decision\"\n        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n        inspect:\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n        transform: |\n          1. Call convergence.cjs once on the current review lineage. It returns the graph decision and the stop_decision object.\n          2. Record the decision as one of CONTINUE, STOP_ALLOWED, STOP_BLOCKED.\n          3. Preserve raw graph signals and blockers for reducer rollup and blocked-stop evidence.\n          4. Normalize blockers to both JSON array and CSV forms for downstream stop handling.\n          5. Set graph_stop_blocked = true only when graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\".\n        bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"review\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\" --depth-mode \"{depth_mode}\" --stop-decision --config-path \"{state_paths.config}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\" --iteration-count \"{iteration_count}\" --security-sensitive-fix-scope \"{security_sensitive_fix_scope}\" --fix-replay-required-rows \"{fix_completeness_replay_required_rows}\" --fix-replay-passing-rows \"{fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows}\" --iteration \"{current_iteration}\" {convergence_write_arg}'\n        note: \"The script is the only place the stop decision is computed. step_check_convergence branches on its stop_decision output. On a BLOCKED decision, {convergence_write_arg} passes --record-blocked-stop on a live run, which makes the script append the deep_review.blocked_stop_recorded event for this iteration through the append gateway itself, once per iteration and blocker set, so a leaf that never reaches step_emit_blocked_stop still leaves the block in the ledger. It recor