config\"\n          - stop_candidate: \"true when graph_decision == STOP_ALLOWED, else false\"\n          - graph_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of graph_signals_json\"\n          - blocked_stop_record: \"Present only when stop_decision.decision == BLOCKED: status recorded, already_recorded or failed, the run, the recoveryStrategy code, the recoveryHint and the gateResults rows the event carries.\"\n        on_blocked_stop_record_failed: \"When blocked_stop_record.status == failed the script exits with the gateway status after printing the decision. Treat it as a gateway refusal under state_write_protocol.refusal_handling: halt, and never write the event by hand.\"\n\n      step_check_convergence:\n        action: \"Branch on the stop decision that convergence.cjs computed in step_graph_convergence\"\n        algorithm: |\n          The whole stop decision is computed by convergence.cjs from the review config, the state log, the findings registry and the coverage graph. This step performs no arithmetic and never recomputes or overrides the result.\n          The ratio signals leave out every iteration that is not evidence-bearing (thought, error, timeout), and stuck_count is loop_counters_json.stuckCount.\n          The script applies this fixed order, first match wins:\n          1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap is evaluated before every veto, the claim-adjudication veto included; failed legal-stop gates are recorded in stop_decision.blockedBy as synthesis evidence.\n          1a. After 3 consecutive failed iterations (status error or timeout), halt the loop and enter synthesis with stop reason error and partial findings.\n          2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n          3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue.\n      step_frontier_admit:\n        action: \"Admit this iteration's review frontier_proposal rows as sub-target nodes before