{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TTxZpSGa2CU6Cb3ybHm31G","type":"tool_result","content":"        return false;\n      }\n      return true;\n    }\n  };\n  if (process.platform === 'win32') {\n    return probe(numericPid);\n  }\n  return probe(-numericPid) || probe(numericPid);\n}\n\nfunction collectOpenLineages(records) {\n  const open = new Map();\n  const spawnedPids = new Map();\n  for (const record of records) {\n    if (!isRecord(record) || typeof record.label !== 'string' || !record.label) {\n      continue;\n    }\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/README.md:49:| `fanout-run.cjs` | Runs research or review fan-out lineages through CLI subprocesses. `--status` prints a read-only per-lineage table from the run's status ledger, and `--stop` ends a live run from a second process. |\n.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:42:>    - `stop_policy` (default `convergence` unless `--stop-policy=max-iterations` is present)\n.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:111:| `--stop-policy` | `convergence` \\| `max-iterations` | See Stop Policy Flag below. |\n.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:116:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior synthesis as `research/synthesis-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_questions_answered` at once, so add questions to `research/inbox.jsonl` before you extend, or create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:137:`--stop-policy <convergence|max-iterations>` selects whether convergence may stop the loop early. The default `convergence` stops at legal convergence or `config.maxIterations`, whichever comes first; `max-iterations` treats convergence as telemetry only and forces the loop to continue until `config.maxIterations`, which is useful for forced-depth runs.\n.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:42:>    - `stop_policy` (default `convergence` unless `--stop-policy=max-iterations` is present)\n.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:104:| `--stop-policy` | `convergence` \\| `max-iterations` | See Stop Policy Flag below. |\n.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:109:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessionId` and generation, records one `run_extended` ledger event and keeps the prior review report as `review/review-report-v{generation}-r{continuedFromRun}.md`. The run must be complete, so use `--lineage-mode=resume` for an unfinished one. Refused with fan-out. The extension keeps the stop policy and convergence mode the run was created with, and a flag passed beside `--extend` does not change them. Under `stopPolicy: convergence` an extension with nothing new can re-stop on `all_dimensions_clean` at once, and an expansive run whose frontier is already drained can re-stop on `frontier_drained` the same way, so create a run you mean to extend with `--convergence-mode=off` or `--stop-policy=max-iterations`. |\n.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:131:`--stop-policy <convergence|max-iterations>` (invocation form `--stop-policy=convergence|max-iterations`) selects whether convergence may stop the loop early.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"bdac924a-e674-4135-af62-678a8439571c","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:13:20.789Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"        return false;\n      }\n  