{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChEj4NygQn6S1A47CAuWn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CwVnPNyyuXkxeG12PKJvQa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 60,95p .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-salvage.md; sed -n 112,122p .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md; P=specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode; grep -n \"pass evidence\\|passEvidence\\|unexamined\\|lineage block\\|claimed\" $P/spec.md $P/tasks.md $P/implementation-summary.md | cut -c1-240 | head -12","description":"Read catalog and packet claims"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2074,"cache_read_input_tokens":270103,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2074},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"79f31a85-e3eb-4c0d-ad62-c2d1cadffd55","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:23:40.995Z","request_id":"req_011ChEj4NpG9kawYdVVRMgCp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CwVnPNyyuXkxeG12PKJvQa":{"command":"sed -n 60,95p .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-salvage.md; sed -n 112,122p .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md; P=specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode; grep -n \"pass evidence\\|passEvidence\\|unexamined\\|lineage block\\|claimed\" $P/spec.md $P/tasks.md $P/implementation-summary.md | cut -c1-240 | head -12","description":"Read catalog and packet claims"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CwVnPNyyuXkxeG12PKJvQa","type":"tool_result","content":"### Pass Evidence\n\n`passEvidence(log, commits)` judges each committed pass from the runner's own log instead of the\nrow the model wrote. A pass is the tool calls between the previous gateway commit and its own;\nthe run-start commit only opens the first window. Calls are timed from opencode events\n(epoch ms, placed by the call's start time) or claude assistant events (ISO stamps). A shell\ncall counts as a source read when one of its commands prints or searches files. Each pass row\ncarries `toolCalls`, `sourceReads`, `commitGapMs`, `skewMs` (the row's stamp minus commit time),\n`findings`, `unexamined` and `reasons`. A pass is `unexamined: true` for any of these reasons:\n\n| Reason | Condition |\n|---|---|\n| `future_stamp` | The row's stamp is later than the gateway commit |\n| `no_reads_no_findings` | No source read and zero findings |\n| `batched_commit` | Committed under 15 s after the previous commit with no tool call between |\n\nA log with no timed event, such as a plain-text log, cannot place a call in a pass, so its\ncounts are null rather than zero, and a pass no rule flags reads as `unexamined: null`, not\nclean, while a count it needs is unknown.\n\n`readLineageCommits(lineageDir)` reads the lineage's gateway frames from\n`deep-research-ledger/frames` or `deep-review-ledger/frames`: the run start, and each iteration\nrow with its commit time, its stamp and its findings count. The stamp is the model's claim: the\nrow's `claimedTimestamp`, else its own `timestamp`, else the event's `occurred_at`. The gateway\nkeeps a research row's stamp as `claimedTimestamp`, and a review frame keeps the model's record\nwhole, so both are judged by the stamp the model wrote. A frame with neither falls back to the\nevent time. A torn frame is skipped.\n`readLineagePassSummary` feeds the fan-out progress row. It judges every lineage log on disk\nplus the running attempt's stdout, and returns `iterations` (distinct committed iterations),\n`lastCommitAt` and `flaggedPasses`. `flaggedPasses` is null while any pass cannot be judged, and\none untimed attempt log, such as a plain-text log from an older run, leaves every pass's call\ncounts unknown.\n\n---\n\npending-question and quota checks read that log's final answer, the last `result` event's text,\nso a completion marker or quota phrase quoted inside a tool result does not decide them.\n\nAfter a lineage exits, whatever its exit code, the runner writes the lineage block of that\nlineage's config from the root config: `generation` (the root's), `parentSessionId` (the root's\n`sessionId`) and `lineageMode: new`. A research config nests them under `lineage`, and a review\nconfig keeps them flat. Every other field, the lineage's own session id among them, is kept.\nThe model writes that config from the workflow template, which knows nothing of the fan-out, so\nruntimes used to fill these fields differently. When the root config is missing or lacks a\n`generation` or `sessionId`, nothing is written.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"44e1cd1c-3ad4-414b-860a-1fb01c6c3c8c","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:23:41.946Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### Pass Evidence\n\n`passEvidence(log, commits)` judges each committed pass from the runner's own log instead of the\nrow the model wrote. A pass is the tool calls between the previous gateway commit and its own;\nthe run-start commit only opens the first window. Calls are timed from opencode events\n(epoch ms, placed by the call's start time) or claude assistant events (ISO stamps). A shell\ncall counts as a source read when one of its commands prints or searches files. Each pass row\ncarries `toolCalls`, `sourceReads`, `commitGapMs`, `skewMs` (the row's stamp minus commit time),\n`findings`, `unexamined` and `reasons`. A pass is `unexamined: true` for any of these reasons:\n\n| Reason | Condition |\n|---|---|\n| `future_stamp` | The row's stamp is later than the gateway commit |\n| `no_reads_no_findings` | No source read and zero findings |\n| `batched_commit` | Committed under 15 s after the previous commit with no tool call between |\n\nA log with no timed event, such as a plain-text log, cannot place a call in a pass, so its\ncounts are null rather than zero, and a pass no rule flags reads as `unexamined: null`, not\nclean, while a count it needs is unknown.\n\n`readLineageCommits(lineageDir)` reads the lineage's gateway frames from\n`deep-research-ledger/frames` or `deep-review-ledger/frames`: the run start, and each iteration\nrow with its commit time, its stamp and its findings count. The stamp is the model's claim: the\nrow's `claimedTimestamp`, else its own `timestamp`, else the event's `occurred_at`. The gateway\nkeeps a research row's stamp as `claimedTimestamp`, and a review frame keeps the model's record\nwhole, so both are judged by the stamp the model wrote. A frame with neither falls back to the\nevent time. A torn frame is skipped.\n`readLineagePassSummary` feeds the fan-out progress row. It judges every lineage log on disk\nplus the running attempt's stdout, and returns `iterations` (distinct committed iterations),\n`lastCommitAt` and `flaggedPasses`. `flaggedPasses` is null while any pass cannot be judged, and\none untimed attempt log, such as a plain-text log from an older run, leaves every pass's call\ncounts unknown.\n\n---\n\npending-question and quota checks read that log's final answer, the last `result` event's text,\nso a completion marker or quota phrase quoted inside a tool result does not decide them.\n\nAfter a lineage exits, whatever its exit code, the runner writes the lineage block of that\nlineage's config from the root config: `generation` (the root's), `parentSessionId` (the root's\n`sessionId`) and `lineageMode: new`. A research config nests them under `lineage`, and a review\nconfig keeps them flat. Every other field, the lineage's own session id among them, is kept.\nThe model writes that config from the workflow template, which knows nothing of the fan-out, so\nruntimes used to fill these fields differently. When the root config is missing or lacks a\n`generation` or `sessionId`, nothing is written.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CwVnPNyyuXkxeG12PKJvQa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
