lus `--only-lineage LABEL`. The command prints\n`{status, stopped, survivors}`, each entry `{label, pid}`, and exits 0 with `status: ok`, or 2\nwith `status: partial` when a lineage still answers. The pool reads a `stopped` row as a closed\nlineage, so its rerun is not requeued as an orphan or charged a retry.\n\nThe bootstrap forwards SIGHUP beside SIGINT and SIGTERM, the signal a closed terminal or a\ndropped SSH session sends. The runner stops its lineages and exits 129 on SIGHUP, 130 on SIGINT\nand 143 on SIGTERM. The TSX child also polls its parent pid every second: when the bootstrap dies,\neven by SIGKILL, which is never forwarded, the child stops its lineages as it would on a\n.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:42:>    - `stop_policy` (default `convergence` unless `--stop-policy=max-iterations` is present)\n.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:104:| `--stop-policy` | `convergence` \\| `max-iterations` | See Stop Policy Flag below. |\n.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:109:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sessio\n.skilled/commands/deep/review.md:131:`--stop-policy <convergence|max-iterations>` (invocation form `--stop-policy=convergence|max-iterations`) selects whether convergence may stop the loop early.\n.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:42:>    - `stop_policy` (default `convergence` unless `--stop-policy=max-iterations` is present)\n.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:111:| `--stop-policy` | `convergence` \\| `max-iterations` | See Stop Policy Flag below. |\n.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:116:| `--extend` | positive integer, as `--extend=N` | Extends a completed run in place by `N` iterations, lineage mode `completed-continue`. The run keeps its `sess\n.skilled/commands/deep/research.md:137:`--stop-policy <convergence|max-iterations>` selects whether convergence may stop the loop early. The default `convergence` stops at legal convergence