{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018aSnnGneYjSfAToQqXbvGR","type":"tool_result","content":"skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md:158:The contract-level check above is illustrative; it is the review-specific 9-gate bundle that actually gates STOP. When that bundle fails, the workflow does not silently override STOP to CONTINUE -- `convergence.cjs`, run with `--record-blocked-st\nskills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:140:`convergence.cjs` records the following row in `deep-review-state.jsonl` whenever the legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP. `step_graph_convergence` in `deep-review.yaml` runs it with `--record-blocked-stop` (live run only; a dry run passes `--read-onl\nskills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:456:> **GATE MODEL, two naming conventions mapped to one authoritative set.** The authoritative producer is `convergence.cjs`, which the `step_graph_convergence` step in `deep-review.yaml` runs with `--record-blocked-stop` (live run only; a dry run passes \nskills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:232:If the legal-stop decision tree returns `blocked`, the `blocked_stop` JSONL event MUST be in the state log before the loop continues. `convergence.cjs` records it: the workflow runs it with `--record-blocked-stop` (live run only; a dry run passes `--r\nskills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-jsonl.md:198:When the review legal-stop decision tree returns `blocked`, `convergence.cjs` records a first-class `blocked_stop` event instead of silently overriding STOP to CONTINUE. The workflow runs it with `--record-blocked-stop` (live run only; a dry run passes `--re\nskills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-jsonl.md:263:`convergence.cjs` writes this row itself. The workflow's convergence step passes `--record-blocked-stop` with `--stop-decision` (live run only; a dry run passes `--read-only` instead, so it appends no blocked-stop row, persists no snapshot and writes no ob\nskills/system-deep-loop/runtime/references/script-interface-contract.md:63:- `status.cjs`, `query.cjs` and `convergence.cjs` accept `--read-only` and read the coverage database. Existing files use the module's read-only SQLite opener. When both WAL side files are absent, the coverage opener reads a header-adjusted byte buffer. O\nskills/system-deep-loop/runtime/references/script-interface-contract.md:66:- In convergence, `--read-only` disables `--persist-snapshot`. Nonempty coverage results report `data.snapshotPersistence: \"not_requested\"` even if persistence was requested. Empty coverage returns before adding that field.\nskills/system-deep-loop/runtime/references/script-interface-contract.md:94:Additional args: `--iteration`, `--persist-snapshot`, `--read-only`, `--record-blocked-stop`.\nskills/system-deep-loop/runtime/references/script-interface-contract.md:100:`--record-blocked-stop` needs `--stop-decision`, loop type `research` or `review` and a positive `--iteration`, and is refused with `--read-only`. On a BLOCKED stop decision it appends the mode's blocked-stop event (`blocked_stop` for research, `deep_rev\nskills/system-deep-loop/runtime/references/script-interface-contract.md:116:Additional args: `--query-type`, optional `--limit`, `--node-id`, `--max-depth`, `--read-only`.\nskills/system-deep-loop/runtime/references/script-interface-contract.md:126:Additional args: `--read-only`.\nskills/system-deep-loop/runtime/references/script-interface-contract.md:162:- `/doctor:deep-loop` calls status, query and convergence with `--read-only`. Its route is `add-only` only because the workflow writes its packet-local state log.\nskills/system-deep-loop/runtime/references/integration-points.md:69:`/doctor:deep-loop` calls status, query and convergence with `--read-only`. Its route is `add-only` only because the workflow writes its packet-local state log.\nskills/system-deep-loop/runtime/references/integration-points.md:73:| `deep-loop` | `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/database/deep-loop-graph.sqlite` (read through `--read-only`) | `add-only` (packet-local state log only) |\nskills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/convergence-script.md:61:`--record-blocked-stop` makes the command record a blocked research or review stop itself, so a leaf that reads a BLOCKED decision and skips the recording step still leaves a state row. It needs `--stop-decision` and `--iteration` as a p\nskills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/convergence-script.md:81:| `tests/integration/convergence-blocked-stop.vitest.ts` | Integration | `--record-blocked-stop`: one row per run and blocker set, a new row for a changed blocker set, a failed command when the gateway refuses, nothing without the flag, \nskills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/convergence-script.md:82:| `tests/integration/convergence-review-blocked-stop.vitest.ts` | Integration | `--record-blocked-stop` for review: one `deep_review.blocked_stop_recorded` event the gateway accepts, no second event for the same run, a block only the gra","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"971b56ea-8c36-469b-a03a-c483a41880f5","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:25:57.757Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/protocol/loop-state-and-gates.md:158:The contract-level check above is illustrative; it is the review-specific 9-gate bundle that actually gates STOP. When that bundle fails, the workflow does not silently override STOP to CONTINUE -- `convergence.cjs`, run with `--record-blocked-st\nskills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md:140:`convergence.cjs` records the following row in `deep-review-state.jsonl` whenever the legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP. `step_graph_c