/integration/convergence-blocked-stop.vitest.ts` | Integration | `--record-blocked-stop`: one row per run and blocker set, a new row for a changed blocker set, a failed command when the gateway refuses, nothing without the flag, \nskills/system-deep-loop/runtime/feature-catalog/script-entry-points/convergence-script.md:82:| `tests/integration/convergence-review-blocked-stop.vitest.ts` | Integration | `--record-blocked-stop` for review: one `deep_review.blocked_stop_recorded` event the gateway accepts, no second event for the same run, a block only the gra","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018aSnnGneYjSfAToQqXbvGR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChEjEojj9hwHM2LbacUHm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0185cKLuuqrrAJiB49j9SRDC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration; sed -n 140,175p .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md","description":"Read review blocked-stop row doc"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2822,"cache_read_input_tokens":288430,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2822},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"c3ad0177-4b38-4d9d-b38d-e5151dfb0232","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:26:01.716Z","request_id":"req_011ChEjEoZK3NVaCNFsrv7Vd","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0185cKLuuqrrAJiB49j9SRDC":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration; sed -n 140,175p .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/convergence/convergence.md","description":"Read review blocked-stop row doc"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0185cKLuuqrrAJiB49j9SRDC","type":"tool_result","content":"`convergence.cjs` records the following row in `deep-review-state.jsonl` whenever the legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP. `step_graph_convergence` in `deep-review.yaml` runs it with `--record-blocked-stop` (live run only; a dry run passes `--read-only` instead, so it appends no blocked-stop row, persists no snapshot and writes no observability event), and on a BLOCKED decision it appends a `deep_review.blocked_stop_recorded` event through the append gateway, which projects to this row. The workflow never writes it by hand. The gate names and their shapes are load-bearing, the reducer reads them verbatim:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"event\",\n  \"event\": \"blocked_stop\",\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"run\": 5,\n  \"blockedBy\": [\"dimensionCoverageGate\", \"p0ResolutionGate\"],\n  \"gateResults\": {\n    \"convergenceGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"score\": 0.72 },\n    \"dimensionCoverageGate\": {\n      \"pass\": false,\n      \"covered\": [\"correctness\", \"security\", \"traceability\"],\n      \"missing\": [\"maintainability\"]\n    },\n    \"p0ResolutionGate\": { \"pass\": false, \"activeP0\": 1 },\n    \"evidenceDensityGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"avgEvidencePerFinding\": 1.6 },\n    \"hotspotSaturationGate\": { \"pass\": true },\n    \"claimAdjudicationGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"activeP0P1\": 2 },\n    \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"securitySensitive\": false, \"requiredRows\": 0, \"passingRows\": 0 },\n    \"candidateCoverageGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"searchDebt\": [], \"missing\": [] },\n    \"graphlessFallbackGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"mode\": \"graph_available\", \"missing\": [], \"unavailabilityReason\": \"\" }\n  },\n  \"graphBlockerDetail\": [],\n  \"recoveryStrategy\": \"Dispatch the next iteration at the maintainability dimension and re-check after resolving the remaining P0.\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T15:02:00Z\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-03-24T10-00-00Z\",\n  \"generation\": 1\n}\n```\n\n- `blockedBy`: array of gate names that failed (string[], never structured objects). Empty when STOP is legal, in which case no `blocked_stop` event is emitted.\n- `gateResults`: named sub-records keyed by `convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, and `graphlessFallbackGate`. This is the full 9-gate set `convergence.cjs` records. Each sub-record has a `pass` boolean plus gate-specific fields (score, covered/missing, activeP0, avgEvidencePerFinding, activeP0P1, securitySensitive, requiredRows, passingRows, searchDebt, mode, unavailabilityReason). The reducer reads these verbatim and does not coerce shapes. `candidateCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` are v2-rollout gates, they pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive (no search debt, graph available).\n- `graphBlockerDetail`: array of structured graph blockers copied from the latest graph convergence decision. Empty when graph convergence did not veto STOP.\n- `recoveryStrategy`: human-readable one-liner describing what the next iteration should do before another stop attempt.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"3b1f1a59-2310-424d-866f-5dd41705c7d7","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:26:01.866Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"`convergence.cjs` records the following row in `deep-review-state.jsonl` whenever the legal-stop decision tree vetoes STOP. `step_graph_convergence` in `deep-review.yaml` runs it with `--record-blocked-stop` (live run only; a dry run passes `--read-only` instead, so it appends no blocked-stop row, persists no snapshot and writes no observability event), and on a BLOCKED decision it appends a `deep_review.blocked_stop_recorded` event through the append gateway, which projects to this row. The workflow never writes it by hand. The gate names and their shapes are load-bearing, the reducer reads them verbatim:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"event\",\n  \"event\": \"blocked_stop\",\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"run\": 5,\n  \"blockedBy\": [\"dimensionCoverageGate\", \"p0ResolutionGate\"],\n  \"gateResults\": {\n    \"convergenceGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"score\": 0.72 },\n    \"dimensionCoverageGate\": {\n      \"pass\": false,\n      \"covered\": [\"correctness\", \"security\", \"traceability\"],\n      \"missing\": [\"maintainability\"]\n    },\n    \"p0ResolutionGate\": { \"pass\": false, \"activeP0\": 1 },\n    \"evidenceDensityGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"avgEvidencePerFinding\": 1.6 },\n    \"hotspotSaturationGate\": { \"pass\": true },\n    \"claimAdjudicationGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"activeP0P1\": 2 },\n    \"fixCompletenessReplayGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"securitySensitive\": false, \"requiredRows\": 0, \"passingRows\": 0 },\n    \"candidateCoverageGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"searchDebt\": [], \"missing\": [] },\n    \"graphlessFallbackGate\": { \"pass\": true, \"mode\": \"graph_available\", \"missing\": [], \"unavailabilityReason\": \"\" }\n  },\n  \"graphBlockerDetail\": [],\n  \"recoveryStrategy\": \"Dispatch the next iteration at the maintainability dimension and re-check after resolving the remaining P0.\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-24T15:02:00Z\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-03-24T10-00-00Z\",\n  \"generation\": 1\n}\n```\n\n- `blockedBy`: array of gate names that failed (string[], never structured objects). Empty when STOP is legal, in which case no `blocked_stop` event is emitted.\n- `gateResults`: named sub-records keyed by `convergenceGate`, `dimensionCoverageGate`, `p0ResolutionGate`, `evidenceDensityGate`, `hotspotSaturationGate`, `claimAdjudicationGate`, `fixCompletenessReplayGate`, `candidateCoverageGate`, and `graphlessFallbackGate`. This is the full 9-gate set `convergence.cjs` records. Each sub-record has a `pass` boolean plus gate-specific fields (score, covered/missing, activeP0, avgEvidencePerFinding, activeP0P1, securitySensitive, requiredRows, passingRows, searchDebt, mode, unavailabilityReason). The reducer reads these verbatim and does not coerce shapes. `candidateCoverageGate` and `graphlessFallbackGate` are v2-rollout gates, they pass trivially when the review-depth-v2 search path is inactive (no search debt, graph available).\n- `graphBlockerDetail`: array of structured graph blockers copied from the latest graph convergence decision. Empty when graph convergence did not veto STOP.\n- `recoveryStrategy`: human-readable one-liner describing what the next iteration should do before another stop attempt.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0185cKLuuqrrAJiB49j9SRDC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
