{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BivqStUjHRQgrnNjKgUthF","type":"tool_result","content":"      step_graph_upsert:\n        action: \"Project canonical review coverage plus optional graphEvents into graph nodes and edges, then upsert it\"\n        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n        transform: |\n          1. Read the latest iteration JSONL record after reducer completion.\n          2. Seed one stable DIMENSION node for every configured review dimension, falling back to correctness, security, traceability, and maintainability.\n          3. Seed one stable FILE node for every latest-record filesReviewed entry and emit a COVERS edge from each latest-record dimension to each reviewed file.\n          4. Merge optional graphEvents nodes after normalizing type = uppercase(event.kind || event.nodeKind || event.type); keep only DIMENSION, FILE, FINDING, EVIDENCE, REMEDIATION, BUG_CLASS, INVARIANT, PRODUCER, CONSUMER, TEST.\n          5. Merge optional graphEvents edges after normalizing relation = uppercase(event.relation); keep only COVERS, EVIDENCE_FOR, CONTRADICTS, RESOLVES, CONFIRMS, ESCALATES, IN_DIMENSION, IN_FILE.\n          6. Emit nodes as { id, type, name, iteration, metadata } and edges as { id, relation, sourceId, targetId, metadata }, deduplicated by id.\n          7. Discard malformed or unknown optional events without discarding canonical dimension and file coverage.\n          8. Do not hand-build finding evidence: upsert.cjs reads iteration {current_iteration}'s finding rows from its delta and the findingDetails of its state record, and adds one FINDING node per finding plus an EVIDENCE_FOR edge to the FILE node of each finding's file:line ref. A leaf finding node whose id wraps the finding id folds onto that node, and an edge to a node neither the batch nor the graph declares is skipped and reported in rejectedOrphanEdges.\n        bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{session_id}\\\" --nodes '{graph_nodes_json}' --edges '{graph_edges_json}' --state-log \\\"{state_paths.state_log}\\\" --delta-dir \\\"{state_paths.delta_dir}\\\" --iteration \\\"{current_iteration}\\\"\"\n        note: \"Invoke the runtime script directly. Canonical iteration fields provide baseline coverage; graphEvents add richer evidence.\"\n        outputs:\n          - graph_nodes_json: \"JSON array of canonical and optional review graph nodes\"\n          - graph_edges_json: \"JSON array of canonical and optional review graph edges\"\n\n      # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Iteration ───\n      gate_post_iteration:\n        applies_to: confirm\n        type: approval_gate\n        purpose: \"Show iteration findings and get approval for next step\"\n        present: |\n          ## Review Iteration {current_iteration} Results\n\n          **Dimensions**: {dimensions}\n          **New Findings**: {findings_count} (P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2})\n          **newFindingsRatio**: {newFindingsRatio}\n          **Status**: {status}\n          **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n          **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n          **Traceability**: {traceability_checks.summary}\n          **Stuck Count**: {stuck_count}\n\n          **Recent Iteration Summary**:\n          {last_3_summaries}\n\n          Options:\n          A) Continue to next iteration\n          B) Continue with adjusted focus: [user provides]\n          C) Stop loop and synthesize\n          D) Cancel entirely\n        wait_for: \"User response\"\n        after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n        on_A: { proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n        on_B: { action: \"Set next_dimension to user's choice in strategy.md\", proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n        on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n        on_D: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n\n      step_update_tracking:\n        action: \"Update loop tracking variables\"\n        set:\n          current_iteration: \"{current_iteration + 1}\"\n        log: \"Iteration {N} complete. Dimensions: {dimensions}. newFindingsRatio: {newFindingsRatio}. Findings: P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2}.\"\n\n      step_loop_decision:\n        action: \"Return to step_read_state for next iteration\"\n        goto: step_read_state\n\n  # ════════\n  # PHASE 3: SYNTHESIS\n  # ════════","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"d13cfa2b-c63f-40e6-9451-97b61dd2c670","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:29:58.310Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"      step_graph_upsert:\n        action: \"Project canonical review coverage plus optional graphEvents into graph nodes and edges, then upsert it\"\n        fanout_graph_store: 'When config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir is bound, or SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID is set, this run is a fan-out lineage and its coverage graph store is {artifact_dir}/graph-db, inside the lineage write surface. The fan-out runner exports DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR to that directory. Run this step against it and never skip it as a write outside the lineage; when DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR is absent from the environment, prefix the command with DEEP_LOOP_COVERAGE_DB_DIR=\"{artifact_dir}/graph-db\".'\n        dry_run_boundary: \"state-mutation\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n        transform: |\n          1. Read the latest iteration JSONL record after reducer completion.\n          2. Seed one stable DIMENSION node for every configured review dimension, falling back to correctness, security, traceability, and maintainability.\n          3. Seed one stable FILE node for every latest-record filesReviewed entry and emit a COVERS edge from each latest-record dimension to each reviewed file.\n          4. Merge optional graphEvents nodes after normalizing type = uppercase(event.kind || event.nodeKind || event.type); keep only DIMENSION, FILE, FINDING, EVIDENCE, REMEDIATION, BUG_CLASS, INVARIANT, PRODUCER, CONSUMER, TEST.\n          5. Merge optional graphEvents edges after normalizing relation = uppercase(event.relation); keep only COVERS, EVIDENCE_FOR, CONTRADICTS, RESOLVES, CONFIRMS, ESCALATES, IN_DIMENSION, IN_FILE.\n          6. Emit nodes as { id, type, name, iteration, metadata } and edges as { id, relation, sourceId, targetId, metadata }, deduplicated by id.\n          7. Discard malformed or unknown optional events without discarding canonical dimension and file coverage.\n          8. Do not hand-build finding evidence: upsert.cjs reads iteration {current_iteration}'s finding rows from its delta and the findingDetails of its state record, and adds one FINDING node per finding plus an EVIDENCE_FOR edge to the FILE node of each finding's file:line ref. A leaf finding node whose id wraps the finding id folds onto that node, and an edge to a node neither the batch nor the graph declares is skipped and reported in rejectedOrphanEdges.\n        bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{session_id}\\\" --nodes '{graph_nodes_json}' --edges '{graph_edges_json}' --state-log \\\"{state_paths.state_log}\\\" --delta-dir \\\"{state_paths.delta_dir}\\\" --iteration \\\"{current_iteration}\\\"\"\n        note: \"Invoke the runtime script directly. Canonical iteration fields provide baseline coverage; graphEvents add richer evidence.\"\n        outputs:\n          - graph_nodes_json: \"JSON array of canonical and optional review graph nodes\"\n          - graph_edges_json: \"JSON array of canonical and optional review graph edges\"\n\n      # ─── APPROVAL GATE: Post-Iteration ───\n      gate_post_iteration:\n        applies_to: confirm\n        type: approval_gate\n        purpose: \"Show iteration findings and get approval for next step\"\n        present: |\n          ## Review Iteration {current_iteration} Results\n\n          **Dimensions**: {dimensions}\n          **New Findings**: {findings_count} (P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2})\n          **newFindingsRatio**: {newFindingsRatio}\n          **Status**: {status}\n          **Cumulative Findings**: P0={p0_count} P1={p1_count} P2={p2_count}\n          **Dimension Coverage**: {dimensions_covered} ({dimension_coverage})\n          **Traceability**: {traceability_checks.summary}\n          **Stuck Count**: {stuck_count}\n\n          **Recent Iteration Summary**:\n          {last_3_summaries}\n\n          Options:\n          A) Continue to next iteration\n          B) Continue with adjusted focus: [user provides]\n          C) Stop loop and synthesize\n          D) Cancel entirely\n        wait_for: \"User response\"\n        after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n        on_A: { proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n        on_B: { action: \"Set next_dimension to user's choice in strategy.md\", proceed_to: step_update_tracking }\n        on_C: { set: { reason: \"manualStop\" }, run_first: record_terminal_gates, proceed_to: phase_synthesis }\n        on_D: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n\n      step_update_tracking:\n        action: \"Update loop tracking variables\"\n        set:\n          current_iteration: \"{current_iteration + 1}\"\n        log: \"Iteration {N} complete. Dimensions: {dimensions}. newFindingsRatio: {newFindingsRatio}. Findings: P0={severity_counts.P0} P1={severity_counts.P1} P2={severity_counts.P2}.\"\n\n      step_loop_decision:\n        action: \"Return to step_read_state for next iteration\"\n        goto: step_read_state\n\n  # ════════\n  # PHASE 3: SYNTHESIS\n  # ════════","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BivqStUjHRQgrnNjKgUthF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
