{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChEja35BzjBcSchC9YToZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SiiscuLJWxXN6gNXGfq25c","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 1200,1240p .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; sed -n 1290,1333p .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | cut -c1-300","description":"Read stop order and stuck recovery handling"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":401,"cache_read_input_tokens":323900,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":401},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"3cf5c57b-7c86-4eb7-8af8-81d345793d4f","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:30:24.340Z","request_id":"req_011ChEja2t2rb7NAtybUzBFW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SiiscuLJWxXN6gNXGfq25c":{"command":"sed -n 1200,1240p .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml; sed -n 1290,1333p .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml | cut -c1-300","description":"Read stop order and stuck recovery handling"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SiiscuLJWxXN6gNXGfq25c","type":"tool_result","content":"          3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue.\n          3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: the vote is telemetry only and the decision is CONTINUE.\n          4. a STOP candidate exists when every dimension is clean (all_dimensions_clean) or the weighted vote passes (composite_converged). The vote cutoffs follow the configured convergenceThreshold. When neither forms and depth_mode == \"expansive\", a run whose frontier holds at least one answered node and none still open or active forms a hard candidate (frontier_drained); a frontier closed with nothing answered forms none. A default run never forms it, and the legal-stop gates below still decide it.\n          4a. if iteration_count < min_iterations: CONTINUE (minIterationsNotReached). min_iterations is config.minIterations, else antiConvergence.minIterations, capped at max_iterations; like research, the floor runs on a candidate before the legal-stop gates.\n          4b. if depth_mode == \"expansive\" and the frontier still holds an open or active node: CONTINUE (frontierOpen). It vetoes every review candidate, all_dimensions_clean included, and never creates a stop.\n          5. the nine legal-stop gates run on a candidate: convergenceGate, dimensionCoverageGate, p0ResolutionGate, evidenceDensityGate, hotspotSaturationGate, claimAdjudicationGate, fixCompletenessReplayGate, candidateCoverageGate, graphlessFallbackGate. Any failed gate gives BLOCKED (blockedStop).\n          6. the graph decision settles the candidate: STOP_ALLOWED keeps STOP, STOP_BLOCKED gives BLOCKED, CONTINUE or a missing graph decision gives CONTINUE.\n          Bind the outputs from stop_decision, where G is stop_decision.gates and I is stop_decision.inputs.review:\n            decision = stop_decision.decision\n            stopReason = stop_decision.stopReason\n            reason = stop_decision.stopReason when it is not null, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\n            reason_detail = stop_decision.reasonDetail\n            weighted_stop_score = stop_decision.weightedStopScore\n            stop_blocked = (stop_decision.decision == \"BLOCKED\")\n            blocked_by_json = stop_decision.blockedBy\n            blocked_by_csv = the members of stop_decision.blockedBy joined with commas\n            convergence_gate_pass = G.convergenceGate.pass\n            convergence_gate_score = G.convergenceGate.score\n            dimension_coverage_gate_pass = G.dimensionCoverageGate.pass\n            dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json = G.dimensionCoverageGate.missing\n            dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json = the configured review dimensions that are not in G.dimensionCoverageGate.missing\n            p0_resolution_gate_pass = G.p0ResolutionGate.pass\n            active_p0_count = G.p0ResolutionGate.activeP0\n            evidence_density_gate_pass = G.evidenceDensityGate.pass\n            avg_evidence_per_finding = I.evidenceBackedP0P1, the count of active P0 and P1 findings that carry file:line evidence\n            hotspot_saturation_gate_pass = G.hotspotSaturationGate.pass\n            claim_adjudication_gate_pass = G.claimAdjudicationGate.pass\n            claim_adjudication_active_count = I.activeP0 plus I.activeP1\n            fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass = G.fixCompletenessReplayGate.pass\n            security_sensitive_fix_scope = I.securitySensitiveFixScope\n            fix_completeness_replay_required_rows = I.fixReplayRequiredRows\n            fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows = I.fixReplayPassingRows\n            candidate_coverage_gate_pass = G.candidateCoverageGate.pass\n            candidate_coverage_search_debt_json = I.searchDebt\n            candidate_coverage_missing_json = the I.requiredBugClasses entries that are not in I.candidateCovered\n            graphless_fallback_gate_pass = G.graphlessFallbackGate.pass\n            graphless_fallback_mode = I.graphCoverageMode\n            graphless_fallback_missing_json = the I.requiredBugClasses entries that are not in I.fallbackCoveredBugClasses\n            graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason = the explicit reason when I.graphCoverageMode == \"unavailable_blocked\", else empty string\n            graph_blocker_detail_json = graph_blockers_json\n            recovery_strategy = one line naming the next review action for the gates in stop_decision.blockedBy: blocked_stop_record.recoveryHint when present, else built as follows. When claimAdjudicationGate is listed: \"Reviewer must add typed claim-adjudication packets (claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger) for every active P0/P1 finding before STOP is allowed.\" When stop_decision.reasonDetail == \"graphStopBlocked\": \"Resolve review coverage-graph blockers before stopping.\" When candidateCoverageGate and graphlessFallbackGate both fail, combine their guidance. When I.unfinishedCoreProtocols is non-empty, name them. When I.unfinishedCoreProtocols is non-empty and traceability_in_run is true, also say the last iteration under the cap is reserved for them, each needing file:line evidence.\n      step_handle_convergence:\n        action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n        if_consecutive_failures:\n          applies_to: confirm\n          when: \"stop_decision.reasonDetail == 'consecutiveFailures'. This branch runs instead of if_stop.\"\n          gate_consecutive_failures:\n            type: approval_gate\n            purpose: \"In confirm mode, ask the operator Retry / Skip / Cancel before synthesis starts.\"\n            present: |\n              **{consecutive_failure_count} iterations in a row failed.**\n\n              Options:\n              A) Retry: dispatch the next iteration with the same dimension\n              B) Skip: dispatch the next iteration with the next dimension\n              C) Cancel: end the run with no synthesis\n            wait_for: \"User response\"\n            after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n            on_A: { set: { decision: \"CONTINUE\" }, proceed_to: step_normalize_pause_events }\n            on_B: { action: \"Advance next_dimension to the next uncovered dimension in strategy.md\", set: { decision: \"CONTINUE\" }, proceed_to: step_normalize_pause_events }\n            on_C: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n          note: \"The failure count is rebuilt from the state log, so this gate asks again after each further failed iteration and stops asking once an iteration completes.\"\n        if_stop:\n          record_terminal_gates:\n            when: \"Run once, immediately before control jumps to phase_synthesis: in if_existing_terminal_path, in the divergent pivot's if_failed and on_error branches, and in every confirm-mode manualStop exit (on_C) into phase_synthesis: both divergent pivot gates, gate_pre_iteration and the post\n            bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/terminal-gates.cjs --config-path \"{state_paths.config}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"'\n            note: \"The script computes all three gates from the config, state log and registry: evidence by the evidenceDensityGate rule, coverage by the dimensionCoverageGate rule, and scope by matching every open finding's file against reviewScopeFiles. Never judge a gate from the findings yoursel\n            on_error: \"When the script exits non-zero or prints status error, fail closed: bind terminal_gate_results_json to three rows, evidence, scope and coverage, each with status fail, reasonCode gate-script-error and evidenceDigest the sha256 of the script's error text, and bind failed_requir\n            evaluate: |\n              terminal_stop_reason = reason when it is maxIterationsReached, maxDurationReached, manualStop or error, else \"converged\". Read reason, never stopReason: every manual stop sets reason to manualStop while stopReason may still hold blockedStop or stuckRecovery\n            outputs:\n              - terminal_gate_results_json: \"Tool terminal_gate_results_json: three rows {gateId, status, reasonCode, evidenceDigest} in the order evidence, scope, coverage\"\n              - failed_required_gate_ids: \"Tool failed_required_gate_ids: the gateIds whose status is fail, in that order; [] when all pass\"\n              - terminal_stop_reason: \"From evaluate\"\n            append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.terminal_gates_recorded\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"stopReason\":\"{terminal_stop_reason}\",\"gateResults\":{terminal_gate_results_json},\"faile\n            log: \"Terminal gates recorded at stop {terminal_stop_reason}. Failed required gates: {failed_required_gate_ids}\"\n          branch_on: \"convergence_mode == 'divergent' AND stop_decision.reasonDetail == 'all_dimensions_clean'\"\n          if_divergent_eligible:\n            eligibility_contract:\n              required_decision: \"STOP\"\n              eligible_reasons: [all_dimensions_clean]\n              excluded_reasons: [maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached]\n              fail_closed: \"Any missing or ambiguous reason uses if_existing_terminal_path without preparing a pivot. The nine legal-stop gates have already run and remain unchanged.\"\n              frontier_gate: \"Under depth_mode == 'expansive' the pivot is eligible only once registry.frontier holds no open or active node. The frontierOpen stop veto already returns CONTINUE while one is open, so this gate records the order rather than adding a second check. A candidate the pivot\n            steps:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc8dabb8-c714-45be-8a95-93ed45ba2410","uuid":"6fdcb797-b4b1-4e99-868f-c31cc0fcd5f8","timestamp":"2026-11-20T19:30:24.505Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"          3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue.\n          3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: the vote is telemetry only and the decision is CONTINUE.\n          4. a STOP candidate exists when every dimension is clean (all_dimensions_clean) or the weighted vote passes (composite_converged). The vote cutoffs follow the configured convergenceThreshold. When neither forms and depth_mode == \"expansive\", a run whose frontier holds at least one answered node and none still open or active forms a hard candidate (frontier_drained); a frontier closed with nothing answered forms none. A default run never forms it, and the legal-stop gates below still decide it.\n          4a. if iteration_count < min_iterations: CONTINUE (minIterationsNotReached). min_iterations is config.minIterations, else antiConvergence.minIterations, capped at max_iterations; like research, the floor runs on a candidate before the legal-stop gates.\n          4b. if depth_mode == \"expansive\" and the frontier still holds an open or active node: CONTINUE (frontierOpen). It vetoes every review candidate, all_dimensions_clean included, and never creates a stop.\n          5. the nine legal-stop gates run on a candidate: convergenceGate, dimensionCoverageGate, p0ResolutionGate, evidenceDensityGate, hotspotSaturationGate, claimAdjudicationGate, fixCompletenessReplayGate, candidateCoverageGate, graphlessFallbackGate. Any failed gate gives BLOCKED (blockedStop).\n          6. the graph decision settles the candidate: STOP_ALLOWED keeps STOP, STOP_BLOCKED gives BLOCKED, CONTINUE or a missing graph decision gives CONTINUE.\n          Bind the outputs from stop_decision, where G is stop_decision.gates and I is stop_decision.inputs.review:\n            decision = stop_decision.decision\n            stopReason = stop_decision.stopReason\n            reason = stop_decision.stopReason when it is not null, else stop_decision.reasonDetail\n            reason_detail = stop_decision.reasonDetail\n            weighted_stop_score = stop_decision.weightedStopScore\n            stop_blocked = (stop_decision.decision == \"BLOCKED\")\n            blocked_by_json = stop_decision.blockedBy\n            blocked_by_csv = the members of stop_decision.blockedBy joined with commas\n            convergence_gate_pass = G.convergenceGate.pass\n            convergence_gate_score = G.convergenceGate.score\n            dimension_coverage_gate_pass = G.dimensionCoverageGate.pass\n            dimension_coverage_gate_missing_json = G.dimensionCoverageGate.missing\n            dimension_coverage_gate_covered_json = the configured review dimensions that are not in G.dimensionCoverageGate.missing\n            p0_resolution_gate_pass = G.p0ResolutionGate.pass\n            active_p0_count = G.p0ResolutionGate.activeP0\n            evidence_density_gate_pass = G.evidenceDensityGate.pass\n            avg_evidence_per_finding = I.evidenceBackedP0P1, the count of active P0 and P1 findings that carry file:line evidence\n            hotspot_saturation_gate_pass = G.hotspotSaturationGate.pass\n            claim_adjudication_gate_pass = G.claimAdjudicationGate.pass\n            claim_adjudication_active_count = I.activeP0 plus I.activeP1\n            fix_completeness_replay_gate_pass = G.fixCompletenessReplayGate.pass\n            security_sensitive_fix_scope = I.securitySensitiveFixScope\n            fix_completeness_replay_required_rows = I.fixReplayRequiredRows\n            fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows = I.fixReplayPassingRows\n            candidate_coverage_gate_pass = G.candidateCoverageGate.pass\n            candidate_coverage_search_debt_json = I.searchDebt\n            candidate_coverage_missing_json = the I.requiredBugClasses entries that are not in I.candidateCovered\n            graphless_fallback_gate_pass = G.graphlessFallbackGate.pass\n            graphless_fallback_mode = I.graphCoverageMode\n            graphless_fallback_missing_json = the I.requiredBugClasses entries that are not in I.fallbackCoveredBugClasses\n            graphless_fallback_unavailability_reason = the explicit reason when I.graphCoverageMode == \"unavailable_blocked\", else empty string\n            graph_blocker_detail_json = graph_blockers_json\n            recovery_strategy = one line naming the next review action for the gates in stop_decision.blockedBy: blocked_stop_record.recoveryHint when present, else built as follows. When claimAdjudicationGate is listed: \"Reviewer must add typed claim-adjudication packets (claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger) for every active P0/P1 finding before STOP is allowed.\" When stop_decision.reasonDetail == \"graphStopBlocked\": \"Resolve review coverage-graph blockers before stopping.\" When candidateCoverageGate and graphlessFallbackGate both fail, combine their guidance. When I.unfinishedCoreProtocols is non-empty, name them. When I.unfinishedCoreProtocols is non-empty and traceability_in_run is true, also say the last iteration under the cap is reserved for them, each needing file:line evidence.\n      step_handle_convergence:\n        action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n        if_consecutive_failures:\n          applies_to: confirm\n          when: \"stop_decision.reasonDetail == 'consecutiveFailures'. This branch runs instead of if_stop.\"\n          gate_consecutive_failures:\n            type: approval_gate\n            purpose: \"In confirm mode, ask the operator Retry / Skip / Cancel before synthesis starts.\"\n            present: |\n              **{consecutive_failure_count} iterations in a row failed.**\n\n              Options:\n              A) Retry: dispatch the next iteration with the same dimension\n              B) Skip: dispatch the next iteration with the next dimension\n              C) Cancel: end the run with no synthesis\n            wait_for: \"User response\"\n            after_gate_refresh_lock: gate_defaults.after_gate_refresh_lock\n            on_A: { set: { decision: \"CONTINUE\" }, proceed_to: step_normalize_pause_events }\n            on_B: { action: \"Advance next_dimension to the next uncovered dimension in strategy.md\", set: { decision: \"CONTINUE\" }, proceed_to: step_normalize_pause_events }\n            on_C: { action: \"Cancel workflow\", status: \"CANCELLED\", release_lock: step_release_lock }\n          note: \"The failure count is rebuilt from the state log, so this gate asks again after each further failed iteration and stops asking once an iteration completes.\"\n        if_stop:\n          record_terminal_gates:\n            when: \"Run once, immediately before control jumps to phase_synthesis: in if_existing_terminal_path, in the divergent pivot's if_failed and on_error branches, and in every confirm-mode manualStop exit (on_C) into phase_synthesis: both divergent pivot gates, gate_pre_iteration and the post\n            bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/terminal-gates.cjs --config-path \"{state_paths.config}\" --state-log \"{state_paths.state_log}\" --registry-path \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"'\n            note: \"The script computes all three gates from the config, state log and registry: evidence by the evidenceDensityGate rule, coverage by the dimensionCoverageGate rule, and scope by matching every open finding's file against reviewScopeFiles. Never judge a gate from the findings yoursel\n            on_error: \"When the script exits non-zero or prints status error, fail closed: bind terminal_gate_results_json to three rows, evidence, scope and coverage, each with status fail, reasonCode gate-script-error and evidenceDigest the sha256 of the script's error text, and bind failed_requir\n            evaluate: |\n              terminal_stop_reason = reason when it is maxIterationsReached, maxDurationReached, manualStop or error, else \"converged\". Read reason, never stopReason: every manual stop sets reason to manualStop while stopReason may still hold blockedStop or stuckRecovery\n            outputs:\n              - terminal_gate_results_json: \"Tool terminal_gate_results_json: three rows {gateId, status, reasonCode, evidenceDigest} in the order evidence, scope, coverage\"\n              - failed_required_gate_ids: \"Tool failed_required_gate_ids: the gateIds whose status is fail, in that order; [] when all pass\"\n              - terminal_stop_reason: \"From evaluate\"\n            append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.terminal_gates_recorded\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"stopReason\":\"{terminal_stop_reason}\",\"gateResults\":{terminal_gate_results_json},\"faile\n            log: \"Terminal gates recorded at stop {terminal_stop_reason}. Failed required gates: {failed_required_gate_ids}\"\n          branch_on: \"convergence_mode == 'divergent' AND stop_decision.reasonDetail == 'all_dimensions_clean'\"\n          if_divergent_eligible:\n            eligibility_contract:\n              required_decision: \"STOP\"\n              eligible_reasons: [all_dimensions_clean]\n              excluded_reasons: [maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused, maxDurationReached]\n              fail_closed: \"Any missing or ambiguous reason uses if_existing_terminal_path without preparing a pivot. The nine legal-stop gates have already run and remain unchanged.\"\n              frontier_gate: \"Under depth_mode == 'expansive' the pivot is eligible only once registry.frontier holds no open or active node.